{
	chapter_group.3CB0832AAD20D6D8.title: "&6Your Kingdom"
	chapter_group.2EAAE7CFEA1F0754.title: "&cA Hero's Path"
	chapter_group.1903F3C70B0F9E81.title: "&5Paths of Magic"
	chapter_group.045D1965A5997F27.title: "&bWorks and Wonders"
	task.6C0EA7BBA9AC5269.title: "Welcome to Ancient Kingdoms"
	quest.6CBF14462DF3EBD3.title: "Ancient Kingdoms"
	quest.6CBF14462DF3EBD3.quest_subtitle: "Three roads out of one door"
	quest.6CBF14462DF3EBD3.quest_desc: [
		"This is a medieval world with a &6kingdom&r to raise, &da shelf of magic&r to learn,"
		"and &cdragons, dungeons and bosses&r for anyone who would rather fight than build."
		""
		"You spawned as one of ten &6Origins&r. Arachnid, Avian, Blazeborn, Merling and the"
		"rest each come with their own powers and drawbacks, and the Origins screen in"
		"your inventory lists what yours can do."
		""
		"Treat this book as a map rather than a rulebook. The four groups on the left"
		"can be read in any order, and nothing in one is locked behind another."
		""
		"&7Changing origin later takes an Orb of Origin, which only staff can hand out.&r"
	]
	quest.24031C0AFBB324AD.title: "Every Book at Once"
	quest.24031C0AFBB324AD.quest_subtitle: "Akashic Tome"
	quest.24031C0AFBB324AD.quest_desc: [
		"Most mods in this pack ship a guidebook, and each one takes a slot. Sneak-right-click"
		"a guidebook onto the &6Akashic Tome&r and the tome swallows it; open the tome and"
		"pick which book you want to read."
		""
		"&7Botania, Ars Nouveau, Blood Magic, Occultism and Primal Magick all have one.&r"
	]
	task.4CE4C27AE82AB38B.title: "Read the three controls"
	quest.05449A6B0E4C87DA.title: "The Controls"
	quest.05449A6B0E4C87DA.quest_subtitle: "Three keys this pack adds"
	quest.05449A6B0E4C87DA.quest_desc: [
		"Three things this pack does that vanilla does not, all worth knowing on day one."
		""
		"&6Claims:&r press &6M&r for the map, right-click a chunk and choose Claim. Nobody"
		"else can build, break or open chests inside it. Every player has an allowance."
		""
		"&6Ultimine:&r hold &6`&r and break one block of a vein or one log of a tree, and"
		"the rest comes with it, for the same hunger as mining by hand."
		""
		"&6Carry On:&r sneak-right-click a chest, furnace or machine with an empty hand to"
		"pick it up with everything still inside. Most animals can be carried the same way."
	]
	quest.02F6BDAF6C8F26C2.title: "Pockets That Keep Up"
	quest.02F6BDAF6C8F26C2.quest_subtitle: "Sophisticated Backpacks"
	quest.02F6BDAF6C8F26C2.quest_desc: [
		"Open a &6Backpack&r with a keybind, without taking it off, and fit it later with"
		"magnets, auto-pickup, filters and a feeding slot."
		""
		"&7Dye it once you own more than one, so the right pack is the one you grab.&r"
	]
	quest.3685603DBF27ABDD.title: "The Road Back"
	quest.3685603DBF27ABDD.quest_subtitle: "A stone to return to"
	quest.3685603DBF27ABDD.quest_desc: [
		"Place a &6Waystone&r at home and right-click it to bind it. From then on every"
		"other Waystone you touch becomes a place you can jump to, for a little experience."
		""
		"&7A second stone wherever you are digging turns a long walk home into a click.&r"
	]
	quest.3C425F8AADB4789E.title: "A Line Mobs Cannot Cross"
	quest.3C425F8AADB4789E.quest_subtitle: "Mega Torch"
	quest.3C425F8AADB4789E.quest_desc: [
		"Nothing hostile spawns within a wide radius of a &6Mega Torch&r, through walls"
		"and floors included. One near the centre of your build covers the whole site."
		""
		"&7The Dread Lamp from the same mod does the same for passive animals, if squids and"
		"bats keep filling your build.&r"
	]
	quest.06B6897B21AE4E56.title: "A Roof of Your Own"
	quest.06B6897B21AE4E56.quest_subtitle: "The first base"
	quest.06B6897B21AE4E56.quest_desc: [
		"A bed and a crafting table inside four walls, on ground you have claimed, with a"
		"Waystone bound at the door. Everything else in this book starts from here."
		""
		"&7Choose a site with flat, open land nearby. A colony needs a wide footprint, and"
		"founding one next to your house saves moving later.&r"
	]
	chapter.1E6BD8812AD85DD9.title: "Getting Started"
	chapter.1E6BD8812AD85DD9.chapter_subtitle: ["Claim a patch of ground, pick who you are, and find the road home."]
	quest.19C511641C03CE6F.title: "Supplies for a Founding"
	quest.19C511641C03CE6F.quest_subtitle: "The camp that becomes a colony"
	quest.19C511641C03CE6F.quest_desc: [
		"Every colony starts with a &6Supply Camp&r. Placed on a flat patch roughly"
		"&617 by 17&r with no grass, flowers or holes, it unpacks into a few starter"
		"buildings and a chest of tools."
		""
		"There is a Supply Ship version if you would rather begin on water."
		""
		"&7You spawn with one in your kit.&r"
	]
	quest.5BA4581C15097FB2.title: "The Build Tool"
	quest.5BA4581C15097FB2.quest_subtitle: "Every hut is placed with this"
	quest.5BA4581C15097FB2.quest_desc: [
		"Anything MineColonies or Structurize places goes down with the &6Build Tool&r:"
		"pick the building, rotate and shift the preview, then confirm."
		""
		"&7Keep it on your hotbar. Every hut and every upgrade goes through it.&r"
	]
	quest.3685B8075652334D.title: "Plant the Town Hall"
	quest.3685B8075652334D.quest_subtitle: "Where the colony starts"
	quest.3685B8075652334D.quest_desc: [
		"Place the &6Town Hall&r and the ground around it becomes your colony. Citizens,"
		"workers, guards and research all hang off this one block."
		""
		"&7Once placed it cannot be moved, so choose flat, open ground.&r"
	]
	quest.7110EB9A2013C59A.title: "Fill the Order"
	quest.7110EB9A2013C59A.quest_subtitle: "Requests and how to answer them"
	quest.7110EB9A2013C59A.quest_desc: [
		"Workers ask for materials through the &6request system&r. Answer one from the"
		"Town Hall screen, or from a Clipboard in your pocket."
		""
		"&7A builder standing still is almost always a builder with an unanswered request.&r"
	]
	quest.45F423C46B926D5D.title: "Somebody Has to Build It"
	quest.45F423C46B926D5D.quest_subtitle: "Hire your first builder"
	quest.45F423C46B926D5D.quest_desc: [
		"Place a &6Builder's Hut&r and assign a citizen to it. From this point you request"
		"buildings instead of laying them block by block, and the builder works from the"
		"chest inside their hut."
		""
		"&7Three paths open from here: housing and food above, population milestones"
		"straight on, and the colony's own upgrades below.&r"
	]
	quest.6B91B54C09AAF864.title: "A Better Hall"
	quest.6B91B54C09AAF864.quest_subtitle: "Town Hall, level five"
	quest.6B91B54C09AAF864.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrading the &6Town Hall&r raises the ceiling on everything else: how many"
		"citizens you may hold and how far the colony's border reaches. Each level asks for"
		"noticeably better materials than the last."
	]
	quest.398804833DD4CE54.title: "Beds for Newcomers"
	quest.398804833DD4CE54.quest_subtitle: "Residences make citizens"
	quest.398804833DD4CE54.quest_desc: [
		"Population is capped by beds. Build a &6Residence&r and a new citizen arrives to"
		"fill it, so build these ahead of demand rather than behind it."
	]
	quest.083005AA6DBFA653.title: "Two Hammers"
	quest.083005AA6DBFA653.quest_subtitle: "A second builder"
	quest.083005AA6DBFA653.quest_desc: [
		"Two buildings go up at once with a second &6Builder's Hut&r. Each builder works only"
		"from their own hut's chest, so both need stocking."
	]
	quest.47FD193B9683EB39.title: "Guards on the Wall"
	quest.47FD193B9683EB39.quest_subtitle: "A Guard Tower"
	quest.47FD193B9683EB39.quest_desc: [
		"Put an armed citizen on patrol with a &6Guard Tower&r. Raiders come for every colony"
		"eventually, and an unguarded one loses buildings."
		""
		"&7The Barracks in Armies of the Realm is the serious version of this.&r"
	]
	quest.0CA56743BBFA0B95.title: "Five Citizens"
	quest.0CA56743BBFA0B95.quest_subtitle: "A hamlet"
	quest.0CA56743BBFA0B95.quest_desc: [
		"Five people: enough to keep a builder, a forester and a chef busy while you go"
		"and find something interesting."
		""
		"&7Citizens arrive on their own while there are free beds.&r"
	]
	quest.4ABF9788A60C3E74.title: "The Tavern"
	quest.4ABF9788A60C3E74.quest_subtitle: "Visitors, and how to keep them"
	quest.4ABF9788A60C3E74.quest_desc: [
		"Visitors come to the &6Tavern&r, and visitors can be recruited for a price in items,"
		"usually food, iron or a tool, paid from your inventory."
		""
		"Recruiting from the Tavern grows the colony faster than waiting for arrivals."
	]
	quest.35CEAD490C2E7FD4.title: "Teach Them Something New"
	quest.35CEAD490C2E7FD4.quest_subtitle: "Custom recipes at a hut"
	quest.35CEAD490C2E7FD4.quest_desc: [
		"Workers craft only what they have been taught. Open a hut's &6Recipes&r tab and"
		"add one; a torch is the traditional first lesson."
		""
		"&7Taught recipes can include modded items, so the colony can make pack parts for you.&r"
	]
	quest.6FAE5143F37117C9.title: "Ten Citizens"
	quest.6FAE5143F37117C9.quest_subtitle: "A village"
	quest.6FAE5143F37117C9.quest_desc: [
		"At ten the colony starts feeding itself, and the &6research tree&r in the Town Hall"
		"begins offering upgrades worth having."
		""
		"&7The University, where that research is done, is in Colony Production.&r"
	]
	quest.4AE033D5EACA43E5.title: "Feed Them Properly"
	quest.4AE033D5EACA43E5.quest_subtitle: "Cooked food and a Chef"
	quest.4AE033D5EACA43E5.quest_desc: [
		"Citizens eat what the colony stocks, and their happiness follows the quality of it."
		"Keep cooked food in stock, and once the colony has a Chef and a Dining Hall (Colony"
		"Production covers those huts) they sit down to proper meals."
		""
		"&7A colony with no Chef eats raw ingredients and loses happiness at every meal.&r"
	]
	quest.1F33B5AA351FDD75.title: "The Mystical Site"
	quest.1F33B5AA351FDD75.quest_subtitle: "Happiness, bought with materials"
	quest.1F33B5AA351FDD75.quest_desc: [
		"Happiness is a colony stat, and the &6Mystical Site&r raises it: a proud colony works"
		"harder and complains less. Level one is cheap and level five is not."
		""
		"&7Unlocked by research at the University, in Colony Production.&r"
	]
	quest.612860931D03476A.title: "Twenty-Five Citizens"
	quest.612860931D03476A.quest_subtitle: "A town"
	quest.612860931D03476A.quest_desc: [
		"Twenty-five people, all of them fed, housed and employed by you. At this size the"
		"colony needs farms and a cook to stay fed."
	]
	quest.1268211E4BF7E2CC.title: "Five Stars"
	quest.1268211E4BF7E2CC.quest_subtitle: "Mystical Site, maxed"
	quest.1268211E4BF7E2CC.quest_desc: [
		"Take the &6Mystical Site&r to level five for the biggest happiness bonus in the game,"
		"and for a far better chance that your Undertaker can raise the dead. It is a long"
		"build, so queue it and go do something else."
	]
	quest.7CB84DF165E7BA1A.title: "Fifty Citizens"
	quest.7CB84DF165E7BA1A.quest_subtitle: "A proper town"
	quest.7CB84DF165E7BA1A.quest_desc: [
		"Fifty people. The colony now runs on its own schedule, and your job is mostly"
		"keeping the warehouse from running dry."
		""
		"&7Add couriers as you grow, or huts sit idle waiting for deliveries.&r"
	]
	quest.11A0F6A2419AA2BC.title: "Seventy-Five Citizens"
	quest.11A0F6A2419AA2BC.quest_subtitle: "A city"
	quest.11A0F6A2419AA2BC.quest_desc: [
		"Seventy-five is about as large as most colonies ever get."
		""
		"&7A colony this size costs a server real performance. On the official servers,"
		"grow past this point with care.&r"
	]
	quest.228BE2C356E18983.title: "Rest for the Dead"
	quest.228BE2C356E18983.quest_subtitle: "The Graveyard and the Undertaker"
	quest.228BE2C356E18983.quest_desc: [
		"Citizens die. A &6Graveyard&r gives them somewhere to go, an &6Undertaker&r buries"
		"them, and with the right totem the Undertaker can bring one back."
		""
		"&7Morale drops while a body is left lying around.&r"
	]
	quest.3EBB7085CD020802.title: "The Kingdom Stands"
	quest.3EBB7085CD020802.quest_subtitle: "A town that runs itself"
	quest.3EBB7085CD020802.quest_desc: [
		"Housed, fed, guarded and staffed. From here the colony is less a project and more"
		"a place you happen to own."
		""
		"Colony Production puts it to work. Armies of the Realm keeps it standing."
	]
	chapter.29850C3411283A15.title: "The Colony"
	chapter.29850C3411283A15.chapter_subtitle: ["A supply camp, a town hall, and someone willing to swing a hammer."]
	quest.41B84724B5BC7731.title: "Timber"
	quest.41B84724B5BC7731.quest_subtitle: "The Forester"
	quest.41B84724B5BC7731.quest_desc: [
		"Your &6Forester&r clears and replants a stretch of forest, forever. Give them an"
		"axe and saplings or they cannot start."
	]
	quest.74BD9AB71E82F10F.title: "The Post Box"
	quest.74BD9AB71E82F10F.quest_subtitle: "Orders without the walk"
	quest.74BD9AB71E82F10F.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Post Box&r lets you order materials from the warehouse without walking to it,"
		"and a &6Stash&r gives couriers a drop point out in the field. Both are cheap, so"
		"place them where you actually work."
		""
		"&7Gathering huts run along the upper arm of this page and crafting huts along the"
		"lower one; the warehouse and its courier sit at the end of the crafting arm.&r"
	]
	quest.5CB733600F604483.title: "The University"
	quest.5CB733600F604483.quest_subtitle: "Where the research happens"
	quest.5CB733600F604483.quest_desc: [
		"Research happens at the &6University&r. The researchers there work through the tree"
		"and unlock the upgrades the Town Hall lists."
		""
		"&7Stock it with paper and books; most early research asks for both.&r"
	]
	quest.6B4F9920B64EF8E3.title: "Planks by the Stack"
	quest.6B4F9920B64EF8E3.quest_subtitle: "The Sawmill"
	quest.6B4F9920B64EF8E3.quest_desc: [
		"Logs from the forester become planks, sticks, doors and every wooden part the"
		"builder keeps asking for at the &6Sawmill&r. Teach it recipes from the hut's Recipes"
		"tab as the requests come in."
	]
	quest.46528C3DBB1FA6D8.title: "All the Way Down"
	quest.46528C3DBB1FA6D8.quest_subtitle: "A mine that reaches bedrock"
	quest.46528C3DBB1FA6D8.quest_desc: [
		"Keep the shaft going until the Miner hits bedrock, down through the deepslate where"
		"diamonds and the better ores actually live."
		""
		"&7Depth is gated on the Miner's Hut level, so upgrade the hut first.&r"
	]
	quest.78A90E2D7A6F40A7.title: "Down the Shaft"
	quest.78A90E2D7A6F40A7.quest_subtitle: "The Miner"
	quest.78A90E2D7A6F40A7.quest_desc: [
		"Give the &6Miner&r a pickaxe, a shovel, torches and ladders and they dig a proper"
		"shaft and bring back whatever is down there."
	]
	quest.3BD2CD01635D24DB.title: "Cut Stone"
	quest.3BD2CD01635D24DB.quest_subtitle: "The Stonemason"
	quest.3BD2CD01635D24DB.quest_desc: [
		"Bricks, slabs, stairs and pillars come out of the &6Stonemason&r's hut from the miner's"
		"haul, which is most of what a serious build eats."
		""
		"&7Domum Ornamentum blocks come from here too, once taught.&r"
	]
	quest.0EFA8136FBFD3E94.title: "Fields and Furrows"
	quest.0EFA8136FBFD3E94.quest_subtitle: "The Farmer"
	quest.0EFA8136FBFD3E94.quest_desc: [
		"Put a scarecrow in the ground, register the field at the hut, and the &6Farmer&r"
		"works it from then on."
		""
		"&7Research lets one farmer hold several fields.&r"
	]
	quest.2907373BA70E6484.title: "Ore into Ingots"
	quest.2907373BA70E6484.quest_subtitle: "The Smeltery"
	quest.2907373BA70E6484.quest_desc: [
		"Ore goes into the &6Smeltery&r, and so do the scrap and broken tools the colony"
		"generates; metal comes back out of both."
		""
		"&7Ore doubling only arrives at the higher hut levels, so level it up.&r"
	]
	quest.4E7553E2BA2BB183.title: "The Library"
	quest.4E7553E2BA2BB183.quest_subtitle: "Citizens who learn"
	quest.4E7553E2BA2BB183.quest_desc: [
		"Citizens study at the &6Library&r and get better at their jobs: faster work, fewer"
		"mistakes, better yields."
	]
	quest.21C72F087C170D75.title: "Off the Dock"
	quest.21C72F087C170D75.quest_subtitle: "The Fisher"
	quest.21C72F087C170D75.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &6Fisher&r on open water for a steady supply of food that costs no farmland"
		"and no animals. The hut has to sit at the water's edge, within casting reach."
	]
	quest.6B8D7B003A7F6B46.title: "Ancient Tomes"
	quest.6B8D7B003A7F6B46.quest_subtitle: "The Enchanter"
	quest.6B8D7B003A7F6B46.quest_desc: [
		"Experience drained from other citizens goes into scrolls and enchanted books at the"
		"&6Enchanter&r."
		""
		"&7Ancient Tomes from dungeon loot push a book past its normal cap.&r"
	]
	quest.1A54D88D2514625B.title: "The Anvil Rings"
	quest.1A54D88D2514625B.quest_subtitle: "The Blacksmith"
	quest.1A54D88D2514625B.quest_desc: [
		"Tools and armour for the rest of the colony come from the &6Blacksmith&r, so the"
		"guards no longer ask you for swords. Between them the Blacksmith and the Mechanic"
		"cover most modded components as well."
	]
	quest.545D35D40E2840B5.title: "Every Kind of Herd"
	quest.545D35D40E2840B5.quest_subtitle: "Cows, sheep, chickens, pigs, rabbits"
	quest.545D35D40E2840B5.quest_desc: [
		"Build the whole set of &6herder huts&r. Between them the colony makes its own meat,"
		"wool and leather without you touching an animal."
		""
		"&7Each herder needs a fenced pen and two animals to start.&r"
	]
	quest.330E9A2FBECCF0B1.title: "Bread in the Morning"
	quest.330E9A2FBECCF0B1.quest_subtitle: "The Baker"
	quest.330E9A2FBECCF0B1.quest_desc: [
		"Wheat becomes bread at the &6Baker&r, and with a few taught recipes pastries, pies"
		"and cakes. Happiness tracks meal quality, not just calories."
	]
	quest.41592F4B2D9023C4.title: "Rot It Down"
	quest.41592F4B2D9023C4.quest_subtitle: "The Composter"
	quest.41592F4B2D9023C4.quest_desc: [
		"Spare crops go into the &6Composter&r and come out as compost for the florist to"
		"plant in and the farmer to spread on the fields. It also soaks up the surplus a"
		"working colony throws off."
	]
	quest.4DA8454B3709381B.title: "The Dining Hall"
	quest.4DA8454B3709381B.quest_subtitle: "Where the colony eats"
	quest.4DA8454B3709381B.quest_desc: [
		"Raw food from every other hut reaches the &6Dining Hall&r, where a Waiter serves it to"
		"the whole colony."
		""
		"&7The Chef's Kitchen next door is where the cooking actually happens, and this pack"
		"gives it a second recipe: eight planks around a Farmer's Delight cabinet.&r"
	]
	quest.13D6A092E34C6065.title: "Flowers for Dye and Petals"
	quest.13D6A092E34C6065.quest_subtitle: "The Florist"
	quest.13D6A092E34C6065.quest_desc: [
		"Flowers grow in the &6Florist&r's mushroom-lit greenhouse: the supply line for dyes,"
		"banners, and every Botania recipe that eats petals."
		""
		"&7They plant in compost, so the Composter comes first.&r"
	]
	quest.46B393AB9F0AEE14.title: "Grind It Down"
	quest.46B393AB9F0AEE14.quest_subtitle: "The Crusher"
	quest.46B393AB9F0AEE14.quest_desc: [
		"Blocks the colony has too much of go into the &6Crusher&r and come out as blocks it"
		"needs: cobble to gravel to sand, bones to meal. Set what it grinds in the hut's"
		"interface or it idles."
	]
	quest.5DC55D8D1F9B20FF.title: "The Warehouse"
	quest.5DC55D8D1F9B20FF.quest_subtitle: "Everything ends up here"
	quest.5DC55D8D1F9B20FF.quest_desc: [
		"Every hut pulls from the &6Warehouse&r and pushes into it; it is the colony's shared"
		"inventory. A full warehouse jams the whole colony, so add racks as it fills."
	]
	quest.473798112B5A0663.title: "Somebody to Fetch It"
	quest.473798112B5A0663.quest_subtitle: "The Courier"
	quest.473798112B5A0663.quest_desc: [
		"With a &6Courier&r running between the warehouse and every hut that needs something,"
		"the colony finally runs without you in it."
		""
		"&7One courier for every four or five working huts is about right.&r"
	]
	chapter.2859E415477AC1B0.title: "Colony Production"
	chapter.2859E415477AC1B0.chapter_subtitle: ["Lumberjacks, miners and smiths — the huts that make the colony pay for itself."]
	quest.4C16AD2F2E1FE699.title: "The Barracks"
	quest.4C16AD2F2E1FE699.quest_subtitle: "Where guards actually live"
	quest.4C16AD2F2E1FE699.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Barracks&r houses a full garrison in one building instead of scattering single"
		"guards across a dozen towers. It is expensive, so start it before your first"
		"serious raid rather than after."
		""
		"&7Barracks, Archery Range and Combat Academy all need research at the University"
		"first. The garrison runs along the upper row here, the siege engines along the lower.&r"
	]
	quest.782EF1363AC2F708.title: "The Siege Workbench"
	quest.782EF1363AC2F708.quest_subtitle: "Where the big things are made"
	quest.782EF1363AC2F708.quest_desc: [
		"Every Medieval Siege Machine is assembled at the &6Siege Workbench&r: beams, wheels,"
		"counterweights and the engines they become. Make plenty of beams and turret bases;"
		"every engine below eats a pile of both."
	]
	quest.444F1AB550B8435A.title: "The Battering Ram"
	quest.444F1AB550B8435A.quest_subtitle: "For doors that will not open"
	quest.444F1AB550B8435A.quest_desc: [
		"Crewed and pushed up to a wall, a &6Battering Ram&r takes it apart. It is slow and"
		"loud, and it needs friends to push."
	]
	quest.176D00509B95D888.title: "Up and Over"
	quest.176D00509B95D888.quest_subtitle: "Siege ladders and turrets"
	quest.176D00509B95D888.quest_desc: [
		"Your people get on top of a wall with a &6Siege Ladder&r, and a &6Turret Base&r mounts"
		"an engine somewhere permanent."
		""
		"&7A ballista on a turret above the gate covers the whole approach.&r"
	]
	quest.5792DB98315FF48D.title: "The Archery Range"
	quest.5792DB98315FF48D.quest_subtitle: "Train them to shoot"
	quest.5792DB98315FF48D.quest_desc: [
		"Guards assigned as archers train at the &6Archery Range&r and level faster than"
		"they would picking fights on the wall. Ranged guards hold a wall well."
	]
	quest.2A3826A90F875B60.title: "The Ballista"
	quest.2A3826A90F875B60.quest_subtitle: "A very large arrow"
	quest.2A3826A90F875B60.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Ballista&r fires a &6Giant Arrow&r flat and fast, and it is the one engine you"
		"can aim at something moving. The arrows come off the same bench, one per shot."
	]
	quest.6D068E4C339CE04C.title: "The Combat Academy"
	quest.6D068E4C339CE04C.quest_subtitle: "Train them to swing"
	quest.6D068E4C339CE04C.quest_desc: [
		"Knights train at the &6Combat Academy&r, the melee half of the same idea. A guard's"
		"level decides both their damage and their health."
	]
	quest.491B4BE1E5C78256.title: "The Catapult"
	quest.491B4BE1E5C78256.quest_subtitle: "Over the wall, not through it"
	quest.491B4BE1E5C78256.quest_desc: [
		"Stone lobbed in an arc from a &6Catapult&r hits what stands behind a wall instead of"
		"the wall itself, and unlike the Ballista and Culverin it needs no shot crafted at the bench."
	]
	quest.7175BB3028174620.title: "Towers on the Wall"
	quest.7175BB3028174620.quest_subtitle: "A barracks tower"
	quest.7175BB3028174620.quest_desc: [
		"Each &6Barracks Tower&r adds another guard to the garrison and another post for"
		"them to hold. Towers upgrade separately from the barracks itself."
	]
	quest.5E90E029E0A6FA85.title: "Eight Under Arms"
	quest.5E90E029E0A6FA85.quest_subtitle: "A garrison"
	quest.5E90E029E0A6FA85.quest_desc: [
		"Eight guards on the payroll: enough to survive an early raid without you standing"
		"in the gateway yourself."
		""
		"&7Feed and equip them, or they fight like citizens with sticks.&r"
	]
	quest.67C0A5B99F4A24A4.title: "Every Tower Manned"
	quest.67C0A5B99F4A24A4.quest_subtitle: "The full barracks"
	quest.67C0A5B99F4A24A4.quest_desc: [
		"Build out every &6Barracks Tower&r the barracks supports and staff them all. Past"
		"this point raids stop being your problem."
	]
	quest.75630A3906922D6F.title: "The Trebuchet"
	quest.75630A3906922D6F.quest_subtitle: "The one with the counterweight"
	quest.75630A3906922D6F.quest_desc: [
		"Largest of the engines, the &6Trebuchet&r drops a stone from a long way off and does"
		"not care what is between you and the target."
		""
		"&7It needs Counterweights, and it is enormous, so leave it room.&r"
	]
	quest.3E565B67607D0254.title: "Thirty Strong"
	quest.3E565B67607D0254.quest_subtitle: "A standing army"
	quest.3E565B67607D0254.quest_desc: [
		"Thirty guards is a real force and a real drain on the food supply. Check the"
		"warehouse before you recruit this hard."
		""
		"&7Your own Blacksmith can make the guards' equipment.&r"
	]
	quest.74CE35CDDDF4EA78.title: "The Culverin"
	quest.74CE35CDDDF4EA78.quest_subtitle: "Powder and iron"
	quest.74CE35CDDDF4EA78.quest_desc: [
		"Gunpowder arrives with the &6Culverin&r, a cannon that throws a &6Cannonball&r flat"
		"and hard. Reloading takes a while, so aim it downhill."
	]
	quest.4C576F06BF547AC2.title: "Eighty Banners"
	quest.4C576F06BF547AC2.quest_subtitle: "An army, properly"
	quest.4C576F06BF547AC2.quest_desc: [
		"Eighty guards under one town hall, with siege engines parked outside."
		""
		"&7The Colony warns you off growing past seventy-five citizens. An army this size is"
		"the exception, and the server pays for it.&r"
	]
	quest.41BD3FD92CAE40D6.title: "The Mortar"
	quest.41BD3FD92CAE40D6.quest_subtitle: "Straight up, straight down"
	quest.41BD3FD92CAE40D6.quest_desc: [
		"A short, fat barrel that throws almost vertically, so it drops shot into a courtyard"
		"the catapult would overshoot and the trebuchet cannot be aimed at tightly enough."
	]
	quest.0A147DC9EBE22E4A.title: "The Realm Holds"
	quest.0A147DC9EBE22E4A.quest_subtitle: "Nothing gets in"
	quest.0A147DC9EBE22E4A.quest_desc: [
		"Garrison trained, towers manned, engines parked and pointed outward."
		""
		"What is left to fight is in A Hero's Path, and it does not come to you."
	]
	chapter.3815F597DE40AF07.title: "Armies of the Realm"
	chapter.3815F597DE40AF07.chapter_subtitle: ["Guards on the wall, archers on the tower, and something large to knock a gate in."]
	quest.25E0CA985705D766.title: "A Knife in the Kitchen"
	quest.25E0CA985705D766.quest_subtitle: "Farmer's Delight starts here"
	quest.25E0CA985705D766.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Knife&r cuts meat into more meat, strips bark, and is the first tool Farmer's"
		"Delight wants you to have. Flint will do to start; iron when you can spare it."
		""
		"&7Every farming mod in the pack shares this page: the kitchen first, the fields"
		"in the middle, the cellar at the end.&r"
	]
	quest.1EBD6312582AAA53.title: "Pots on the Windowsill"
	quest.1EBD6312582AAA53.quest_subtitle: "Botany Pots"
	quest.1EBD6312582AAA53.quest_desc: [
		"One crop or sapling grows in a &6Botany Pot&r on its own soil, indoors, in a space one"
		"block wide, and a hopper underneath harvests it for you."
		""
		"&7Botany Trees adds saplings, so a pot can farm logs as well as wheat.&r"
	]
	quest.6AC3F09E94A64ABA.title: "Stove and Basket"
	quest.6AC3F09E94A64ABA.quest_subtitle: "Cooking without a campfire"
	quest.6AC3F09E94A64ABA.quest_desc: [
		"Food cooked on a &6Stove&r does not burn, and the stove doubles as a heat source for"
		"the cooking pot. A &6Basket&r holds a harvest and pushes it into whatever is below."
	]
	quest.510D197E124FA0F0.title: "The Cutting Board"
	quest.510D197E124FA0F0.quest_subtitle: "Where the knife gets used"
	quest.510D197E124FA0F0.quest_desc: [
		"Put food on a &6Cutting Board&r and hit it with a knife to get more out of it than"
		"the crafting grid gives. It works on logs, pumpkins and a great many mod ingredients."
	]
	quest.3740D17FE3FA82E9.title: "Pot and Skillet"
	quest.3740D17FE3FA82E9.quest_subtitle: "Cooking Pot and Skillet"
	quest.3740D17FE3FA82E9.quest_desc: [
		"Stews come out of the &6Cooking Pot&r and the &6Skillet&r fries things fast. Both sit"
		"on a heat source and both want a container item nearby."
		""
		"&7You can hold the Skillet and cook from it directly, so it travels well.&r"
	]
	quest.6160B771DECA018A.title: "The Market Stall"
	quest.6160B771DECA018A.quest_subtitle: "Farming for Blockheads"
	quest.6160B771DECA018A.quest_desc: [
		"Seeds, saplings and animals are sold at the &6Market&r for emeralds, the fastest way to"
		"fill a gap in your crop list without walking a thousand blocks."
		""
		"&7Fertilizer from the same mod skips a growth stage across a whole plot.&r"
	]
	quest.13883DD2AAECFB2B.title: "Feed the Herd"
	quest.13883DD2AAECFB2B.quest_subtitle: "Troughs and nests"
	quest.13883DD2AAECFB2B.quest_desc: [
		"Penned animals breed from a &6Feeding Trough&r without you standing there clicking, and"
		"a &6Chicken Nest&r collects eggs. Both cap out, so a pen cannot run away with itself."
	]
	quest.3799A922F8705AD2.title: "Richer Ground"
	quest.3799A922F8705AD2.quest_subtitle: "Compost and rich soil"
	quest.3799A922F8705AD2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Organic Compost&r turns dirt into &6Rich Soil&r, which grows crops faster and never"
		"needs watering. Rotten flesh, bone meal, straw and dirt go into it, all things you"
		"have too much of."
	]
	quest.47A6DF612D4E9346.title: "Croptopia"
	quest.47A6DF612D4E9346.quest_subtitle: "Sixty crops you have never planted"
	quest.47A6DF612D4E9346.quest_desc: [
		"&6Croptopia&r scatters new crops through every biome: tomatoes, corn, rice, coffee,"
		"olives and a long list more. Most are found growing wild first, and the seeds come"
		"from the crop itself, so finding one is the same as owning it."
	]
	quest.7A8F342C24CB1F18.title: "Growthcraft"
	quest.7A8F342C24CB1F18.quest_subtitle: "Rice, hops, grain and bees"
	quest.7A8F342C24CB1F18.quest_desc: [
		"&6Growthcraft&r brings paddy rice, hop vines, grain and its own bee boxes, with a"
		"&6Brew Kettle&r to turn them into something drinkable."
		""
		"&7Rice needs standing water. Hops need a rope to climb.&r"
	]
	quest.27737FCF5F964BBF.title: "A Box of Bees"
	quest.27737FCF5F964BBF.quest_subtitle: "Growthcraft Apiary"
	quest.27737FCF5F964BBF.quest_desc: [
		"Honeycomb, beeswax and candles come from a &6Bee Box&r set under a flowering tree."
		""
		"&7Keep candles in stock. The ritual chapters ask for them often.&r"
	]
	quest.59C9066EA459C1EB.title: "Tea and Coffee"
	quest.59C9066EA459C1EB.quest_subtitle: "Let's Do HerbalBrews"
	quest.59C9066EA459C1EB.quest_desc: [
		"&6HerbalBrews&r grows tea, coffee, lavender and hibiscus and brews them in a kettle"
		"for small, long buffs. Green tea suits a mining trip; coffee suits a fight."
	]
	quest.093E532D5DCAF6DC.title: "Salt, Oil and Cheese"
	quest.093E532D5DCAF6DC.quest_subtitle: "The three things every recipe wants"
	quest.093E532D5DCAF6DC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Salt&r comes from smelting a Croptopia water bottle, &6Olive Oil&r from pressing olives, and"
		"&6Cheese&r from milk. Croptopia's recipe list is built on these three, so get all"
		"of them going before you try anything ambitious."
	]
	quest.5B9FE217747A1D3D.title: "Grapes on the Vine"
	quest.5B9FE217747A1D3D.quest_subtitle: "Let's Do Vinery"
	quest.5B9FE217747A1D3D.quest_desc: [
		"Plant a &6Grapevine&r on loam, let it fruit, and pick the grapes by hand. &6Vinery&r"
		"is a whole small industry hanging off that one plant."
		""
		"&7Loam is made from clay and sand. Grapes will not grow without it.&r"
	]
	quest.7431F7F84CBDB9E4.title: "Press the Apples"
	quest.7431F7F84CBDB9E4.quest_subtitle: "Cider and juice"
	quest.7431F7F84CBDB9E4.quest_desc: [
		"Apples squeezed in the &6Apple Press&r give juice, which ferments into cider. This is"
		"the gentler end of Vinery and it needs no grapes at all."
		""
		"&7Growthcraft apple trees supply the apples in bulk.&r"
	]
	quest.5FDD10669B46A361.title: "The Long Table"
	quest.5FDD10669B46A361.quest_subtitle: "Feed a colony properly"
	quest.5FDD10669B46A361.quest_desc: [
		"Teach your colony's &6Chef&r the recipes from these mods and the whole settlement eats"
		"meals that raise happiness. Open the Chef's Kitchen, go to the Recipes tab and add"
		"them; the Chef handles it from then on."
	]
	quest.37BD4082FF3A42B7.title: "Into the Barrel"
	quest.37BD4082FF3A42B7.quest_subtitle: "Fermentation"
	quest.37BD4082FF3A42B7.quest_desc: [
		"Grapes go into a &6Fermentation Barrel&r with a bottle and come out as wine."
		"Different grapes make different wines with different effects when drunk."
		""
		"&7Wine keeps improving in a Wine Box, so age the good bottles.&r"
	]
	quest.6DCA4B84FEFBC4F7.title: "Beer and Wine Together"
	quest.6DCA4B84FEFBC4F7.quest_subtitle: "A full cellar"
	quest.6DCA4B84FEFBC4F7.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &6Brewingstation&r for beer beside the barrel of wine already ageing, and two of"
		"the pack's four drinks mods are running side by side."
		""
		"&7Each drink carries its own effect, worth checking before a boss fight.&r"
	]
	chapter.36FDE7C02708683F.title: "Hearth and Harvest"
	chapter.36FDE7C02708683F.chapter_subtitle: ["Knives, pots and presses. Every farming mod in the pack, and what each of them is for."]
	quest.7A49A346BA0AD8C7.title: "Put a Roof On It"
	quest.7A49A346BA0AD8C7.quest_subtitle: "Macaw's Roofs"
	quest.7A49A346BA0AD8C7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Macaw's Roofs&r adds sloped roofs in every wood and stone the game has, plus"
		"gutters, awnings and the corner pieces that make them meet cleanly. At six hundred"
		"blocks it is the pack's largest single decoration mod."
	]
	quest.10AA5693F3D01C41.title: "The Architect's Cutter"
	quest.10AA5693F3D01C41.quest_subtitle: "Domum Ornamentum"
	quest.10AA5693F3D01C41.quest_desc: [
		"&6Domum Ornamentum&r is the block set MineColonies builds from: bricks, shingles,"
		"timber framing, all cut on the &6Architect's Cutter&r."
		""
		"&7Timber framing takes two materials, so one recipe covers hundreds of looks.&r"
	]
	quest.58723811DACA4C46.title: "The Construction Wand"
	quest.58723811DACA4C46.quest_subtitle: "Place a whole wall at once"
	quest.58723811DACA4C46.quest_desc: [
		"Look along a surface with a &6Construction Wand&r and it extends in that direction, as"
		"far as the wand's tier allows and your inventory can pay for. Stone, iron, diamond and"
		"infinity wands each reach further than the last."
	]
	quest.4C02F5C9979816D3.title: "Doors and Trapdoors"
	quest.4C02F5C9979816D3.quest_subtitle: "Macaw's Doors"
	quest.4C02F5C9979816D3.quest_desc: [
		"Western doors, barn doors, glass doors, stable doors, and trapdoors to match, all"
		"from the same family of mods."
		""
		"&7The doors are two blocks tall like vanilla's, so they drop into an existing frame.&r"
	]
	quest.4D1FC89306FC4396.title: "Copy and Paste"
	quest.4D1FC89306FC4396.quest_subtitle: "Structurize"
	quest.4D1FC89306FC4396.quest_desc: [
		"&6Structurize&r scans a building into a file with the &6Scan Tool&r and places it"
		"again anywhere with the Build Tool."
		""
		"&7This is also how custom MineColonies styles are made for your own colony.&r"
	]
	quest.5CA3BA3CF60C0412.title: "Let Some Light In"
	quest.5CA3BA3CF60C0412.quest_subtitle: "Macaw's Windows"
	quest.5CA3BA3CF60C0412.quest_desc: [
		"&6Macaw's Windows&r covers shutters, blinds, arrow slits and stained glass in frames"
		"that line up with the roofs. The resizeable windows stretch to fill whatever hole"
		"you left."
	]
	quest.6D4E773A6BE28EA9.title: "Bricks in Five Colours"
	quest.6D4E773A6BE28EA9.quest_subtitle: "Coloured stone and brick"
	quest.6D4E773A6BE28EA9.quest_desc: [
		"The same cutter makes brick and stone brick in colours vanilla never had: sand,"
		"cream, beige, roan and brown. Teach these to the Stonemason and the colony builds in colour"
		"instead of cobble."
	]
	quest.325999F2E3F4B616.title: "Fences and Crossings"
	quest.325999F2E3F4B616.quest_subtitle: "Macaw's Fences and Bridges"
	quest.325999F2E3F4B616.quest_desc: [
		"Highley gates, picket fences, rope bridges and stone arches: the last two mods in"
		"the Macaw's set this pack ships."
		""
		"&7A rope bridge is a few planks and string, and crosses a ravine cleanly.&r"
	]
	quest.4F2C23D4CB46286C.title: "Medieval Dressing"
	quest.4F2C23D4CB46286C.quest_subtitle: "Medieval Deco"
	quest.4F2C23D4CB46286C.quest_desc: [
		"Barrels, crates, figureheads, market props. &6Medieval Deco&r fills a street with"
		"the clutter that makes it look inhabited."
	]
	quest.4EE966263366B39C.title: "Fill and Replace"
	quest.4EE966263366B39C.quest_subtitle: "Substitution blocks"
	quest.4EE966263366B39C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Solid&r and &6Fluid Substitution&r blocks mark where a scanned building should use"
		"whatever is already there instead of a fixed block. A scan full of them fits any"
		"hillside you drop it on."
	]
	quest.24E98B3041865E65.title: "Quark's Odd Blocks"
	quest.24E98B3041865E65.quest_subtitle: "Shingles, thatch, vertical planks"
	quest.24E98B3041865E65.quest_desc: [
		"&6Quark&r quietly adds several hundred building blocks, among them thatch, shingles,"
		"vertical slabs, midori and shale."
		""
		"&7Its Trowel places a random block from your hotbar each swing, so a wall built from"
		"three similar blocks stops looking tiled.&r"
	]
	quest.2F1B19DF3CC2899F.title: "Chairs and Couches"
	quest.2F1B19DF3CC2899F.quest_subtitle: "Handcrafted"
	quest.2F1B19DF3CC2899F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Handcrafted&r is chairs, couches, tables, cupboards and shelves in every wood, and"
		"it is the furniture MineColonies' own builders use."
		""
		"&7MineColonies' own builders place its cupboards and shelves throughout a colony.&r"
	]
	quest.779F3964E67DE547.title: "Hang a Painting"
	quest.779F3964E67DE547.quest_subtitle: "Immersive Paintings"
	quest.779F3964E67DE547.quest_desc: [
		"&6Immersive Paintings&r lets you resize a painting, choose which one you get, and"
		"make one out of a screenshot. No more placing the same painting nine times hoping"
		"for the right roll."
	]
	quest.11A75255C7BB2AA9.title: "Desks and Drawers"
	quest.11A75255C7BB2AA9.quest_subtitle: "Valhelsia Furniture"
	quest.11A75255C7BB2AA9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Valhelsia Furniture&r covers the pieces the other two skip: desks with drawers,"
		"stools, and lamps that give off light. The desks hold items."
	]
	quest.4BBC80BFA9F6C7B5.title: "Food on the Table"
	quest.4BBC80BFA9F6C7B5.quest_subtitle: "Placeable food and items"
	quest.4BBC80BFA9F6C7B5.quest_desc: [
		"Two small mods put food and ordinary items down as blocks: a loaf on a table,"
		"ingots stacked on a shelf, eggs in a basket. Most of it is placed by right-clicking"
		"the item onto a surface rather than crafted."
		""
		"&7Placed items keep their stack, so pick them back up when you need them.&r"
	]
	quest.3FD291E1E0D95BED.title: "Furniture for a Throne Room"
	quest.3FD291E1E0D95BED.quest_subtitle: "Fantasy's Furniture"
	quest.3FD291E1E0D95BED.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fantasy's Furniture&r is themed sets: Royal, Dunmer, Nordic, Necrolord, Venthyr and"
		"Bone. Every piece is made at the &6Furniture Station&r, and one station covers them all."
		""
		"&7The Royal set is what a throne room in this pack is supposed to look like.&r"
	]
	chapter.7AFF50617333F76C.title: "Halls and Homes"
	chapter.7AFF50617333F76C.chapter_subtitle: ["Roofs, furniture and trim — the mods that turn a box with a door into a hall."]
	task.75E3E2BF815EB881.title: "Kill 25 zombies"
	quest.41FB99370D73710A.title: "Paid to Fight"
	quest.41FB99370D73710A.quest_subtitle: "Where money comes from here"
	quest.41FB99370D73710A.quest_desc: [
		"Every hostile mob you kill pays you &6one coin&r, and killing is where most of your"
		"money will come from. There is no ore to sell and no crop to grind. Twenty-five"
		"zombies will do for a start."
		""
		"Spend them with &6/shop&r, which sells food, colony parts, tools, pets and Alex's"
		"Caves maps, and buys surplus on its Sell tab. The &6Market&r beside it lists your"
		"own goods for other players at a price you set. &6Easy Villagers&r, which the rest"
		"of this page covers, gives you trades you own outright and can automate, with"
		"nobody else online."
		""
		"&7Kills are counted per player, so everyone in a party is paid for the same fight.&r"
	]
	quest.530BD5A11479DB1C.title: "The Old Way"
	quest.530BD5A11479DB1C.quest_subtitle: "Trade with a villager"
	quest.530BD5A11479DB1C.quest_desc: [
		"Villagers still work the way they always did, and a librarian with the right book"
		"trades for more than most things in the shop cost."
		""
		"&7Break and replace their workstation until the trade you want appears.&r"
	]
	quest.3EA0527B70408550.title: "Villager in a Box"
	quest.3EA0527B70408550.quest_subtitle: "Easy Villagers"
	quest.3EA0527B70408550.quest_desc: [
		"Pick a villager up with an empty hand and put them in a &6Trader&r block. Their"
		"trades become a screen you click, permanently, indoors, with no wandering off."
	]
	quest.0F5BA4DB0906E780.title: "More Where That Came From"
	quest.0F5BA4DB0906E780.quest_subtitle: "Breeder and Incubator"
	quest.0F5BA4DB0906E780.quest_desc: [
		"Two villagers and food go into a &6Breeder&r and babies come out; an &6Incubator&r grows"
		"the babies up on demand. Carrots or bread keep it going indefinitely."
	]
	quest.39DB3BA6C16C6232.title: "Trades Without You"
	quest.39DB3BA6C16C6232.quest_subtitle: "The Auto Trader"
	quest.39DB3BA6C16C6232.quest_desc: [
		"Set an &6Auto Trader&r on a villager's trade and it runs on its own, pulling from one"
		"side and pushing the result out the other. Find a trade that pays and it makes"
		"emeralds while you are elsewhere."
	]
	quest.0C7CD293CADC48B8.title: "Wealthy"
	quest.0C7CD293CADC48B8.quest_subtitle: "Nine stacks of green"
	quest.0C7CD293CADC48B8.quest_desc: [
		"A wall of emerald blocks, earned rather than found."
		""
		"&7An Auto Trader on a farmer villager is the quickest route here.&r"
	]
	quest.098832F90DA4B6DB.title: "Cure the Cursed"
	quest.098832F90DA4B6DB.quest_subtitle: "The Converter"
	quest.098832F90DA4B6DB.quest_desc: [
		"Zombie villagers are cured in a &6Converter&r without you standing there holding a"
		"splash potion and hoping."
		""
		"&7A cured villager discounts its trades permanently, which repays the golden apple.&r"
	]
	quest.1F15DB0F0385D181.title: "Iron on Tap"
	quest.1F15DB0F0385D181.quest_subtitle: "The Iron Farm block"
	quest.1F15DB0F0385D181.quest_desc: [
		"Three villagers in an &6Iron Farm&r block produce golems, which produce iron, in the"
		"space of one block instead of one chunk."
	]
	chapter.0766EA595AC3EF1D.title: "Coin and Commerce"
	chapter.0766EA595AC3EF1D.chapter_subtitle: ["Coins for kills, a shop to spend them in, and villagers who never sleep."]
	quest.7AD9D56A86E12487.title: "Pick a Shape"
	quest.7AD9D56A86E12487.quest_subtitle: "Simply Swords"
	quest.7AD9D56A86E12487.quest_desc: [
		"&6Simply Swords&r adds fifteen weapon shapes in every vanilla material: katanas,"
		"glaives, rapiers, scythes, warglaives, chakrams. Each shape swings differently,"
		"so try a few before you commit to one."
		""
		"Everything on this row is a plain crafting recipe with no new metals. The column"
		"on the right is where the new metals start."
	]
	quest.5DEA44FAE1C48652.title: "Enchant It Properly"
	quest.5DEA44FAE1C48652.quest_subtitle: "Enchanting Infuser"
	quest.5DEA44FAE1C48652.quest_desc: [
		"Choose the enchantment instead of gambling at the &6Enchanting Infuser&r, paying lapis"
		"for the privilege. The advanced version reaches the same levels a full bookshelf"
		"ring does."
	]
	quest.2AF2CB42A91F7779.title: "Reach and Range"
	quest.2AF2CB42A91F7779.quest_subtitle: "Spartan Weaponry"
	quest.2AF2CB42A91F7779.quest_desc: [
		"&6Spartan Weaponry&r is the other half of the same idea: pikes, halberds,"
		"boomerangs, javelins, longbows and heavy crossbows."
		""
		"&7Its parrying daggers block in the offhand and pair well with a rapier.&r"
	]
	quest.552BD2DA4EE9AA80.title: "Armour With a Face"
	quest.552BD2DA4EE9AA80.quest_subtitle: "Immersive Armors"
	quest.552BD2DA4EE9AA80.quest_desc: [
		"&6Immersive Armors&r adds ten full sets between leather and netherite: warrior,"
		"heavy, robe, prismarine, bone, wither. Each set carries its own effect on top of"
		"its numbers, and the tooltip spells it out."
		""
		"&7Spell scrolls, single-use casts on paper, turn up in the same dungeon chests as"
		"the armour and need no spellbook to use.&r"
	]
	task.4C306B3EB8E1950F.title: "Find any Artifact"
	quest.06F28B4971B8A2E2.title: "Trinkets"
	quest.06F28B4971B8A2E2.quest_subtitle: "Artifacts"
	quest.06F28B4971B8A2E2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Artifacts&r are never crafted. They come out of the mimic chests and campsites"
		"scattered underground: boots that double-jump, hats that see in the dark, belts"
		"that keep you from drowning. They sit in Curios slots and cost you no armour."
	]
	quest.2EFB9A340D3F62DF.title: "Bone and Slime"
	quest.2EFB9A340D3F62DF.quest_subtitle: "The odd sets"
	quest.2EFB9A340D3F62DF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Bone&r armour is cheap and frightens the undead; &6Slime&r armour bounces. Both"
		"are early, and both do something plate does not."
		""
		"&7Bone gear is also a component in one of the pack's summoning rituals.&r"
	]
	quest.593B6CE2022E0060.title: "Demonite"
	quest.593B6CE2022E0060.quest_subtitle: "Soulslike Weaponry begins"
	quest.593B6CE2022E0060.quest_desc: [
		"&6Marium's Soulslike Weaponry&r runs on its own metals. &6Demonite Chunks&r smelt"
		"into &6Crimson Ingots&r, and moonstone comes out of deepslate. Its bosses drop the"
		"rest, and Beasts and Bosses covers those."
	]
	quest.7D90A0092BC0E816.title: "A Full Rack"
	quest.7D90A0092BC0E816.quest_subtitle: "One of each"
	quest.7D90A0092BC0E816.quest_desc: [
		"A blade from Simply Swords, a polearm from Spartan, a named weapon from Fantasy"
		"Weapons, and a matched set of armour hung beside them."
		""
		"&7An armour stand and a painting from Halls and Homes make it an armoury.&r"
	]
	quest.20A540F5DAFAF953.title: "Soul Infused Iron"
	quest.20A540F5DAFAF953.quest_subtitle: "Lost souls, put to work"
	quest.20A540F5DAFAF953.quest_desc: [
		"Combine a &6Lost Soul&r with an iron ingot for a &6Soul Infused Ingot&r, the gate into"
		"the mod's mid-tier gear."
		""
		"&7Lost souls smelt straight out of soul sand, and drop from the mod's dark sorcerers.&r"
	]
	quest.6E60237498774BF2.title: "Netherite, Finally"
	quest.6E60237498774BF2.quest_subtitle: "The gate the rest sits behind"
	quest.6E60237498774BF2.quest_desc: [
		"Three of the mods in this chapter upgrade &lfrom&r a netherite weapon. Until you hold"
		"one, their pages in JEI are a wish list."
		""
		"&7Ancient debris from the Nether: four scrap and four gold per ingot.&r"
	]
	quest.7ADE178DDA9EA016.title: "Blazing Stone"
	quest.7ADE178DDA9EA016.quest_subtitle: "Fantasy Weapons"
	quest.7ADE178DDA9EA016.quest_desc: [
		"&6Blazing Stone&r, made from blaze powder, glowstone and stone, turns a netherite"
		"weapon into one of Fantasy Weapons' sixty named blades at a smithing table: estocs,"
		"dancing blades, dragonslayer halberds."
	]
	quest.0891ABE2D473A970.title: "A Named Blade"
	quest.0891ABE2D473A970.quest_subtitle: "One from the rack"
	quest.0891ABE2D473A970.quest_desc: [
		"Take a netherite weapon, a Blazing Stone and a smithing table, and pick one. There"
		"are sixty, and they do not all fight the same way."
		""
		"&7Fantasy Armor works the same way, but off a Moon Crystal instead.&r"
	]
	quest.6C8D549446412719.title: "Knight's Plate"
	quest.6C8D549446412719.quest_subtitle: "Fantasy Armor"
	quest.6C8D549446412719.quest_desc: [
		"Thirty armour sets in the same style as the weapons: crucible knight, chess board"
		"knight, dragonslayer, dark lord. Each has its own stats and effect, so check them"
		"before you commit the crystal."
	]
	quest.6B97C4E2397924CC.title: "Runic"
	quest.6B97C4E2397924CC.quest_subtitle: "The top of Simply Swords"
	quest.6B97C4E2397924CC.quest_desc: [
		"Combine a &6Runic Tablet&r from a dungeon chest, a netherite Simply Swords weapon and a diamond for a"
		"&6Runic&r weapon, the enchantable, upgradeable end of the mod."
		""
		"&7Runefused Gems take it further still, with crying obsidian.&r"
	]
	chapter.16C1E15AD2D57E08.title: "The Armory"
	chapter.16C1E15AD2D57E08.chapter_subtitle: ["Glaives, katanas, pikes and greatswords — and which mod they came from."]
	task.059569D9D14EAE46.title: "Kill the Ancient Remnant"
	quest.7AAA12290AA7CC74.title: "The Ancient Remnant"
	quest.7AAA12290AA7CC74.quest_subtitle: "Desert site"
	quest.7AAA12290AA7CC74.quest_desc: [
		"A stone guardian buried under the desert, and the gentlest of the eight. Break its"
		"stone plates before they close again."
		""
		"&7The pack's ritual altar can summon it, if you would rather not go looking.&r"
	]
	task.3A6E8401AA8DFACF.title: "Kill the Leviathan"
	quest.4DA81F6F8373D921.title: "The Leviathan"
	quest.4DA81F6F8373D921.quest_subtitle: "Sunken city"
	quest.4DA81F6F8373D921.quest_desc: [
		"A drowned colossus in the ocean's deepest ruin. The fight happens underwater, and"
		"that is the hard part."
		""
		"&7Bring a conduit, or at least respiration and a door.&r"
	]
	task.07BD76E56F28C3AC.title: "Kill the Netherite Monstrosity"
	quest.45FBB802B69F9C29.title: "The Netherite Monstrosity"
	quest.45FBB802B69F9C29.quest_subtitle: "Burning arena"
	quest.45FBB802B69F9C29.quest_desc: [
		"An enormous armoured brute in the Nether that throws lava bombs and shockwaves. It"
		"is slow, and fire resistance is close to mandatory."
		""
		"&7It drops the Infernal Forge, the pickaxe both endgame fusion weapons are built from.&r"
	]
	task.1702F605327F8426.title: "Kill Scylla"
	task.17C0B9655D154D42.title: "Kill Coralssus"
	quest.7ABEFAA8454CA5B3.title: "Scylla and Coralssus"
	quest.7ABEFAA8454CA5B3.quest_subtitle: "The ocean's other two"
	quest.7ABEFAA8454CA5B3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Scylla&r guards the frosted prison; &6Coralssus&r sits in the coral. Neither is as"
		"large as the Leviathan and both hit harder than they look, so take them one at a time."
	]
	task.4F770723B35307B5.title: "Kill Ignis"
	quest.1EF8B1539FE3CCA8.title: "Ignis"
	quest.1EF8B1539FE3CCA8.quest_subtitle: "Ancient factory"
	quest.1EF8B1539FE3CCA8.quest_desc: [
		"The knight of flame, and the hardest of the early fights: fireballs, a flame strike,"
		"and a second phase that changes the rules."
		""
		"&7Ignis drops &6Ignitium&r, the ingot behind its fireproof armour and the Incinerator.&r"
	]
	task.0FB466B33EE30812.title: "Kill Maledictus"
	quest.62A4EEE977063CEF.title: "Maledictus"
	quest.62A4EEE977063CEF.quest_subtitle: "Cursed pyramid"
	quest.62A4EEE977063CEF.quest_desc: [
		"The cursed pharaoh, in a pyramid full of things that were once people. It is fast"
		"and it does not stay where you swing."
		""
		"&7Clear the pyramid first. With its servants alive it is a different fight.&r"
	]
	task.22AF78E0E8EBA2EB.title: "Kill the Harbinger"
	quest.43AC61AD3F70791A.title: "The Harbinger"
	quest.43AC61AD3F70791A.quest_subtitle: "Abandoned village"
	quest.43AC61AD3F70791A.quest_desc: [
		"A gaunt thing that reaps in a wide circle and heals off what it kills. Keep out of"
		"the crowd of its own summons."
		""
		"&7Three wither skulls and a pig at the summoning altar also fetch it.&r"
	]
	task.6E3F48ACF8B08F09.title: "Kill the Ender Guardian"
	quest.5DD36909EE171D3E.title: "The Ender Guardian"
	quest.5DD36909EE171D3E.quest_subtitle: "Ruined citadel"
	quest.5DD36909EE171D3E.quest_desc: [
		"Waiting in the End, in a citadel the dragon never touched. It teleports, it summons"
		"golems, and it does not tire."
		""
		"&7Bring a ranged option for the golems, room to dodge the void runes, and food for a long fight.&r"
	]
	quest.7B9885A9F788AB87.title: "Witherite"
	quest.7B9885A9F788AB87.quest_subtitle: "What the bosses were for"
	quest.7B9885A9F788AB87.quest_desc: [
		"&6Witherite&r drops from the Harbinger and forges the Wither Assault Shoulder Weapon,"
		"the Meat Shredder, the Laser Gatling, and the Mechanical Fusion Anvil that welds the"
		"boss weapons into each other."
	]
	quest.356283A77462DD43.title: "Nothing Left Standing"
	quest.356283A77462DD43.quest_subtitle: "The realm's monsters, answered"
	quest.356283A77462DD43.quest_desc: [
		"Eight arenas cleared, a kingdom's worth of knights put down, and a rack of weapons"
		"that exist only because you did it."
		""
		"Here Be Dragons is the other end of this, and a different kind of fight."
	]
	quest.7D5CA69EF6F80739.title: "The Decaying Kingdom"
	quest.7D5CA69EF6F80739.quest_subtitle: "Soulslike Weaponry's bosses"
	quest.7D5CA69EF6F80739.quest_desc: [
		"A cathedral, a set of champion's graves, a corrupt altar and, down in the Nether, a"
		"ruined kingdom, each with its own boss: the Returning Knight, the Old Champion, the"
		"Monarch of Chaos and the Decaying King."
		""
		"&7Each knight drops a Lord Soul, and the mod's best weapons are smithed from those.&r"
	]
	quest.584CB69543A6C66E.title: "Alex's Mobs"
	quest.584CB69543A6C66E.quest_subtitle: "Ninety animals that were not here before"
	quest.584CB69543A6C66E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Alex's Mobs&r fills the world with real wildlife: grizzlies, gorillas, orcas,"
		"komodo dragons, crimson mosquitoes, bone serpents. The &6Animal Dictionary&r tells"
		"you what each one drops and what tames it."
	]
	quest.409B83FC23CC13F4.title: "The Primordial Caves"
	quest.409B83FC23CC13F4.quest_subtitle: "Things with teeth"
	quest.409B83FC23CC13F4.quest_desc: [
		"A prehistoric layer under the world, complete with the animals to match. The amber"
		"down here holds things worth extracting."
		""
		"&7A dino bowl is an arena with teeth in it, so go in armed.&r"
	]
	quest.00B33015BBD55299.title: "A Lord Soul"
	quest.00B33015BBD55299.quest_subtitle: "The top of the tree"
	quest.00B33015BBD55299.quest_desc: [
		"Beat one of the knights, take its &6Lord Soul&r, and smith it onto a netherite"
		"weapon. Any knight's soul will serve for most of the list; the Crucible Sword is a"
		"strong first choice."
	]
	quest.65203AC9E8F8636F.title: "The Forlorn Hollows"
	quest.65203AC9E8F8636F.quest_subtitle: "The dark one"
	quest.65203AC9E8F8636F.quest_desc: [
		"Vampire bats, a licowitch tower, and a bridge across a canyon that somebody built on"
		"purpose."
		""
		"&7Light does not spread in the Forlorn Hollows, so torches are for placing, not for"
		"seeing by.&r"
	]
	quest.1492BEBE30924B0E.title: "The Abyssal Chasm"
	quest.1492BEBE30924B0E.quest_subtitle: "Under the ocean floor"
	quest.1492BEBE30924B0E.quest_desc: [
		"Deeper than the deep dark and considerably wetter: deep ones, ruins, and pressure"
		"that does not care about your helmet."
		""
		"&7Save this one for last. It needs water breathing and pressure protection.&r"
	]
	task.5F47C648D3EE6F80.title: "Clear every wave of a Gateway"
	quest.6EB92FBA413A2209.title: "Waves Without End"
	quest.6EB92FBA413A2209.quest_subtitle: "A gateway, properly run"
	quest.6EB92FBA413A2209.quest_desc: [
		"Open a &6Gateway&r somewhere you control and clear every wave it throws. The higher"
		"tiers pull from everything in this chapter."
		""
		"&7Bring the colony guards. This is what they are for.&r"
	]
	chapter.5B4D6BA827BB3E32.title: "Beasts and Bosses"
	chapter.5B4D6BA827BB3E32.chapter_subtitle: ["Eight Cataclysm bosses, a decaying kingdom's worth of knights, and the caves."]
	quest.4D47915AE7BB9F13.title: "A Torn Page"
	quest.4D47915AE7BB9F13.quest_subtitle: "Manuscripts"
	quest.4D47915AE7BB9F13.quest_desc: [
		"&6Manuscripts&r turn up in ordinary dungeon and mineshaft loot, and drop from myrmex"
		"and from the mod's own graveyards. Three of them stack into a &6Bestiary&r."
	]
	quest.72853B1AB6BDC38D.title: "Ghosts and Graveyards"
	quest.72853B1AB6BDC38D.quest_subtitle: "The bestiary's quieter pages"
	quest.72853B1AB6BDC38D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ghosts&r haunt the mod's graveyards and pass through walls, and their sword does"
		"the same to armour."
		""
		"&7A ghost chest keeps its contents where nobody else can reach them.&r"
	]
	quest.278F8F6EFC836B67.title: "A Roost on the Hill"
	quest.278F8F6EFC836B67.quest_subtitle: "Find a dragon"
	quest.278F8F6EFC836B67.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fire, Ice&r and &6Lightning&r dragons each have caves and surface roosts, and each"
		"roost is a hoard sitting on a sleeping adult."
		""
		"&7Age matters more than anything, so check the size before you commit.&r"
	]
	quest.6CD8EDC8178D8C67.title: "The Bestiary"
	quest.6CD8EDC8178D8C67.quest_subtitle: "Everything the mod will tell you"
	quest.6CD8EDC8178D8C67.quest_desc: [
		"Ice and Fire's guidebook is the &6Bestiary&r, and it fills in as you meet things. Read"
		"the dragon pages before you go looking for one."
		""
		"&7Sneak-click it into your Akashic Tome so it stops going missing.&r"
	]
	quest.02488CDBA149A0F6.title: "Stymphalian Birds"
	quest.02488CDBA149A0F6.quest_subtitle: "A flock is worse than a boss"
	quest.02488CDBA149A0F6.quest_desc: [
		"They come in dozens, they throw their own feathers at you, and the feathers stick."
		"Those feathers make arrows, so the fight is not wasted."
	]
	quest.15439AFA6835C5D9.title: "Kill a Dragon"
	quest.15439AFA6835C5D9.quest_subtitle: "The fight the mod is named for"
	quest.15439AFA6835C5D9.quest_desc: [
		"Bone, scales, blood and a skull. A grown dragon carries all of it and will use every"
		"bit of the sky to keep it."
		""
		"&7Fight it grounded. A dragon in the air is a different animal entirely.&r"
	]
	quest.7B24E0C56DA06EC5.title: "Silver and Sapphire"
	quest.7B24E0C56DA06EC5.quest_subtitle: "The mod's own ores"
	quest.7B24E0C56DA06EC5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Silver&r generates like iron and &6Sapphire&r like diamond. Silver makes most of"
		"the mod's mid-tier gear, and dragons hoard sapphires, so there are two ways to get them."
	]
	quest.3BB8A5709F46E345.title: "The Dread Lands"
	quest.3BB8A5709F46E345.quest_subtitle: "Ice and Fire's own dimension"
	quest.3BB8A5709F46E345.quest_desc: [
		"A grey world of dread stone and the undead who keep it, reached through a mausoleum"
		"in the overworld. Dread gear is good; getting out again is the part to plan for."
	]
	quest.297163A3EC4866AD.title: "Bone and Scale"
	quest.297163A3EC4866AD.quest_subtitle: "What comes off it"
	quest.297163A3EC4866AD.quest_desc: [
		"&6Dragonbone&r makes weapons; &6Dragonscales&r make armour, one colour set per"
		"dragon. Both are worked on an ordinary crafting table."
		""
		"&7The colours are cosmetic; the stats are the same.&r"
	]
	quest.2CCF7FB8C27BC6E9.title: "An Egg of Your Own"
	quest.2CCF7FB8C27BC6E9.quest_subtitle: "Raise one instead"
	quest.2CCF7FB8C27BC6E9.quest_desc: [
		"Take a &6Dragon Egg&r from a hoard, set it in a nest and light it, and it hatches into a"
		"dragon that grows with you. A &6Dragon Horn&r carries it and a &6Dragon Flute&r calls it back down."
		""
		"&7Keep it fed. A hungry dragon does not grow.&r"
	]
	quest.0BA87C9827345057.title: "The Cyclops Cave"
	quest.0BA87C9827345057.quest_subtitle: "Start small"
	quest.0BA87C9827345057.quest_desc: [
		"Sheep and a chest worth opening sit in a cave guarded by a &6Cyclops&r. It is slow,"
		"enormous, and it will pick you up."
		""
		"&7Aim for its eye. A blinded cyclops cannot target you.&r"
	]
	quest.21BBE8117452D7EA.title: "Trolls Under the Mountain"
	quest.21BBE8117452D7EA.quest_subtitle: "Three kinds, three leathers"
	quest.21BBE8117452D7EA.quest_desc: [
		"Forest, frost and mountain &6Trolls&r live in caves and turn to stone in daylight."
		"Their hides make three sets of armour, and their weapons drop too, hitting harder"
		"than their looks suggest."
	]
	quest.7098112BFBB5D2BD.title: "Build the Forge"
	quest.7098112BFBB5D2BD.quest_subtitle: "Bricks, a core, an input"
	quest.7098112BFBB5D2BD.quest_desc: [
		"Fire bricks around a core with an input make the &6Dragon Forge&r, a small multiblock"
		"that lights only when a living dragon breathes on it. The bricks are stone bricks laid"
		"around blocks of dragon scale, and each element needs its own forge."
	]
	quest.6AE9B05EA453AD7D.title: "Sirens and Sea Serpents"
	quest.6AE9B05EA453AD7D.quest_subtitle: "Do not sail without earplugs"
	quest.6AE9B05EA453AD7D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sirens&r sing sailors off their boats. &6Earplugs&r stop that, and are made before"
		"you meet one, not after."
		""
		"&7Sea serpent scales make tide armour, the best water gear in the pack.&r"
	]
	quest.28C680AE6CC07D43.title: "The Deathworm"
	quest.28C680AE6CC07D43.quest_subtitle: "Under the sand"
	quest.28C680AE6CC07D43.quest_desc: [
		"Under the desert floor lives the &6Deathworm&r. Its chitin makes armour and a gauntlet"
		"that punches things a very long way."
		""
		"&7Deathworm eggs hatch if you carry one in your inventory. A tame one burrows and"
		"fights alongside you.&r"
	]
	quest.216A67DACD8B8AB3.title: "Dragonsteel"
	quest.216A67DACD8B8AB3.quest_subtitle: "The best metal in the pack"
	quest.216A67DACD8B8AB3.quest_desc: [
		"Feed the lit forge iron ingots and dragon blood and it returns &6Dragonsteel&r. Fire, ice"
		"and lightning each have their own, and their own gear."
		""
		"&7A tamed dragon of the matching element, told to attack the forge, keeps it lit.&r"
	]
	quest.6E4983ECC2EC5053.title: "The Hydra"
	quest.6E4983ECC2EC5053.quest_subtitle: "Cut one off and two grow back"
	quest.6E4983ECC2EC5053.quest_desc: [
		"Every head you take off the &6Hydra&r grows back unless the stump is burned. It lives"
		"in a cave lair marked by dead ground and bones outside the entrance, and everything"
		"about the fight is about fire."
	]
	quest.0691F065A8768951.title: "Tamed and Winged"
	quest.0691F065A8768951.quest_subtitle: "Hippogryphs, amphitheres, pixies"
	quest.0691F065A8768951.quest_desc: [
		"Not everything in Ice and Fire has to be killed. &6Hippogryphs&r, &6Amphitheres&r,"
		"&6Hippocampi&r, &6Cockatrices&r and &6Pixies&r all tame, and a hippogryph is the"
		"earliest flying mount in the pack."
	]
	quest.6E6B7C795B58F30E.title: "Dragonsteel Plate"
	quest.6E6B7C795B58F30E.quest_subtitle: "The end of the armour tree"
	quest.6E6B7C795B58F30E.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Dragonsteel&r chestplate, and the three pieces to match it, outclass netherite. Dragon armour for"
		"your own dragon comes from the same ingot."
	]
	quest.59395B19B3B0F1ED.title: "Dragon Rider"
	quest.59395B19B3B0F1ED.quest_subtitle: "The point of all of it"
	quest.59395B19B3B0F1ED.quest_desc: [
		"A grown dragon in dragonsteel armour, with you on its back."
		""
		"&7Sit, then look where you want to go. Landing is the hard part.&r"
	]
	chapter.5C5DD5494EECDDD2.title: "Here Be Dragons"
	chapter.5C5DD5494EECDDD2.chapter_subtitle: ["Manuscripts, roosts and the forge that turns a dead dragon into armour."]
	quest.09FB936DC751A637.title: "A Wider World"
	quest.09FB936DC751A637.quest_subtitle: "Nature's Compass, and fifty new biomes"
	quest.09FB936DC751A637.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oh The Biomes We've Gone&r replaces most of the overworld's biome list with"
		"fifty-odd of its own: bayous, black forests, cika woods, prairies, each with its"
		"own trees and most with their own wood type."
		""
		"A &6Nature's Compass&r finds any of them by name. Right-click it, search for the"
		"biome, and it points at the nearest one and tells you how far it is."
	]
	quest.653FB3B22C88C565.title: "Taverns and Manors"
	quest.653FB3B22C88C565.quest_subtitle: "Dungeons and Taverns"
	quest.653FB3B22C88C565.quest_desc: [
		"&6Dungeons and Taverns&r fills the gaps between the landmarks with taverns, illager"
		"manors, fire watch towers, hamlets and crypts, fifty-eight of them in all."
		""
		"&7Its illager hideouts are a reliable early source of armour.&r"
	]
	quest.1BAE507202BFC237.title: "Not the Village You Remember"
	quest.1BAE507202BFC237.quest_subtitle: "Towns and Towers"
	quest.1BAE507202BFC237.quest_desc: [
		"&6Towns and Towers&r rebuilds villages and pillager outposts in a dozen regional"
		"styles and adds a few the base game never had."
		""
		"&7Its outposts are noticeably harder than vanilla's, so a shield is worth carrying.&r"
	]
	quest.7C0F3963C67CA977.title: "The Castle on the Hill"
	quest.7C0F3963C67CA977.quest_subtitle: "Valhelsia Structures"
	quest.7C0F3963C67CA977.quest_desc: [
		"&6Valhelsia&r builds the castle, a real one with a keep, spawner rooms and a treasury"
		"worth the fight. The same mod places the forge, the witch hut and those enormous trees."
	]
	quest.3E143AA8DE5DD9AB.title: "Somebody Lived Here"
	quest.3E143AA8DE5DD9AB.quest_subtitle: "Structory"
	quest.3E143AA8DE5DD9AB.quest_desc: [
		"&6Structory&r is the quiet one: small, careful ruins with no loot fanfare. An"
		"abandoned chapel, a fire tower, a manor going to seed. Its chests are modest and"
		"its layouts are the point."
	]
	quest.2DC03B577796C9AD.title: "Better Dungeons"
	quest.2DC03B577796C9AD.quest_subtitle: "YUNG's rebuilt the basics"
	quest.2DC03B577796C9AD.quest_desc: [
		"&6YUNG's Better Dungeons&r replaces the plain cobble box with themed dungeons, zombie,"
		"skeleton and spider, each with its own layout and loot."
	]
	quest.7769B7E2560CF8D6.title: "Dungeons Arise"
	quest.7769B7E2560CF8D6.quest_subtitle: "The big ones"
	quest.7769B7E2560CF8D6.quest_desc: [
		"&6When Dungeons Arise&r builds the landmarks: a coliseum, a keep, a pirate ship, and"
		"three heavenly warships that hang in the sky."
		""
		"&7Keep Kayra and the Coliseum are the largest of the set, with several spawner rooms"
		"each, and both are far easier cleared in daylight.&r"
	]
	quest.1898C6E20DD3A7EB.title: "Rooms Under the Rooms"
	quest.1898C6E20DD3A7EB.quest_subtitle: "Ember's Underground Rooms"
	quest.1898C6E20DD3A7EB.quest_desc: [
		"&6Underground Rooms&r hides twenty furnished chambers below the surface: a library,"
		"a jail, a wine cellar, a throne room. They connect, so finding one usually means"
		"finding four."
	]
	quest.48F2640208383A1B.title: "Six Caves That Should Not Exist"
	quest.48F2640208383A1B.quest_subtitle: "Alex's Caves"
	quest.48F2640208383A1B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Alex's Caves&r digs six enormous biomes under the world: magnetic caves, primordial"
		"caves, toxic caves, forlorn hollows, the abyssal chasm, and a cavity made entirely"
		"of confectionery."
		""
		"&7A Cave Biome Map from the shop points at one, and saves a great deal of digging.&r"
	]
	quest.65982A3B0EA742A9.title: "Down Below"
	quest.65982A3B0EA742A9.quest_subtitle: "Blaze rods, quartz and piglin barter"
	quest.65982A3B0EA742A9.quest_desc: [
		"Blaze rods, quartz, ghast tears, and half the reagents the magic chapters are going"
		"to ask for."
		""
		"&7Bring gold ingots to barter with piglins for pearls, string and obsidian.&r"
	]
	quest.178B9B9D5C775312.title: "Into the Candy Cavity"
	quest.178B9B9D5C775312.quest_subtitle: "The strangest of the six"
	quest.178B9B9D5C775312.quest_desc: [
		"Nougat walls, liquorice, a gingerbread town and a witch that hits hard. Most"
		"blocks here can be eaten, and most creatures here are hostile."
	]
	quest.548B844E48D3D36E.title: "The End of the Line"
	quest.548B844E48D3D36E.quest_subtitle: "Cities, ships and a citadel"
	quest.548B844E48D3D36E.quest_desc: [
		"The dragon, the cities, the ships. The End is also where Cataclysm's &6Ender"
		"Guardian&r waits, in a ruined citadel. Everything out here is easier with an elytra."
	]
	quest.04960AD98343CA90.title: "The Deep Dark"
	quest.04960AD98343CA90.quest_subtitle: "An Ancient City"
	quest.04960AD98343CA90.quest_desc: [
		"Still the quietest and most dangerous place in the overworld. Sneak, muffle your"
		"steps with wool, and plan the route before you go in."
		""
		"&7Its loot is the only source of a few enchantments in this pack.&r"
	]
	quest.3B1050478D02E0CE.title: "A City in the Void"
	quest.3B1050478D02E0CE.quest_subtitle: "End City"
	quest.3B1050478D02E0CE.quest_desc: [
		"Shulker shells, an elytra, and the best enchanted gear that generates anywhere in"
		"the world."
		""
		"&7Take every shulker shell you can, and bring blocks to bridge between towers.&r"
	]
	quest.1880BA7D01167C3B.title: "Every Road Walked"
	quest.1880BA7D01167C3B.quest_subtitle: "The realm, charted"
	quest.1880BA7D01167C3B.quest_desc: [
		"Surface, underground, Nether, End and the mirror behind them all."
		""
		"What is left to find is guarded. The rest of this group is about that."
	]
	quest.39A14BF35291D573.title: "The Mirror"
	quest.39A14BF35291D573.quest_subtitle: "Overworld Mirror"
	quest.39A14BF35291D573.quest_desc: [
		"&6Overworld Mirror&r opens a second overworld: the same rules, untouched land, and a"
		"clean set of every structure in this chapter."
		""
		"&7Use it for large-scale mining, so the overworld everyone shares stays intact.&r"
	]
	chapter.52471AA566652BD0.title: "Charting the Realm"
	chapter.52471AA566652BD0.chapter_subtitle: ["Fifty new biomes and eight mods' worth of ruins to walk into."]
	quest.69DA85CC92FB5070.title: "The Lexica Botania"
	quest.69DA85CC92FB5070.quest_subtitle: "A sapling and a book"
	quest.69DA85CC92FB5070.quest_desc: [
		"One sapling and one book make the &6Lexica Botania&r, the mod's in-game manual. New"
		"pages unlock as you build."
		""
		"The spine of this page runs left to right from petals to terrasteel. Everything"
		"hanging off it below is a way of making or carrying mana; the one branch above is"
		"the gear that spends it."
		""
		"&7Sneak-click the book into your Akashic Tome and stop carrying it separately.&r"
	]
	quest.7ED5E23B8E0CB124.title: "Petals"
	quest.7ED5E23B8E0CB124.quest_subtitle: "Sixteen colours of flower"
	quest.7ED5E23B8E0CB124.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mystical Flowers&r grow wild in every colour. Break them for &6Petals&r, the"
		"currency of everything that follows."
		""
		"&7A Flower Pouch keeps sixteen colours in one slot, and is worth making early.&r"
	]
	quest.2748D3FF4B09778A.title: "The Petal Apothecary"
	quest.2748D3FF4B09778A.quest_subtitle: "Cobblestone and petals"
	quest.2748D3FF4B09778A.quest_desc: [
		"Build the &6Petal Apothecary&r, fill it with a water bucket, and throw petals plus a"
		"seed in. Every flower past the mystical ones is made this way, and it does nothing dry."
	]
	quest.29130AE61C03F80A.title: "Explosions and Lava"
	quest.29130AE61C03F80A.quest_subtitle: "The loud generators"
	quest.29130AE61C03F80A.quest_desc: [
		"Primed TNT going off beside an &6Entropinnyum&r pays out; a &6Thermalily&r drinks lava"
		"straight from the source block. Both outproduce an endoflame many times over, and"
		"both need a supply line built for them."
	]
	quest.2D739EB98AA6412C.title: "The Pure Daisy"
	quest.2D739EB98AA6412C.quest_subtitle: "Wood and stone, made alive"
	quest.2D739EB98AA6412C.quest_desc: [
		"Logs and stone around a &6Pure Daisy&r turn into &6Livingwood&r and &6Livingrock&r. It"
		"converts the eight blocks in the ring at its own level, so lay them there and walk"
		"away."
	]
	quest.37CC2AA97A7C7BA0.title: "Feed It Dinner"
	quest.37CC2AA97A7C7BA0.quest_subtitle: "The Gourmaryllis"
	quest.37CC2AA97A7C7BA0.quest_desc: [
		"Cooked food dropped near a &6Gourmaryllis&r becomes mana in proportion to how filling"
		"it was, with a bonus for variety over repetition. It is a good reason to keep the"
		"Hearth and Harvest kitchen running."
	]
	quest.7010C8BAA5A9C1EB.title: "Water and Slime"
	quest.7010C8BAA5A9C1EB.quest_subtitle: "The passive flowers"
	quest.7010C8BAA5A9C1EB.quest_desc: [
		"&6Hydroangeas&r drink water; &6Narslimmus&r eat slimes that spawn near them. Neither"
		"needs feeding by hand, but the Hydroangeas withers after about three days, so plan"
		"to replant."
	]
	quest.41B8AB99473019E6.title: "Pool and Spreader"
	quest.41B8AB99473019E6.quest_subtitle: "Where mana lives and how it moves"
	quest.41B8AB99473019E6.quest_desc: [
		"Mana is stored in a &6Mana Pool&r of livingrock and fired in a straight line by a"
		"&6Mana Spreader&r of livingwood, to wherever the spreader is aimed."
		""
		"&7Aim the Spreader at the Pool. Its range is limited and any solid block breaks the beam.&r"
	]
	quest.285C8FCB4BF48B27.title: "Burn Something"
	quest.285C8FCB4BF48B27.quest_subtitle: "The Endoflame"
	quest.285C8FCB4BF48B27.quest_desc: [
		"Drop coal or charcoal near an &6Endoflame&r and it makes mana. It is slow and cheap,"
		"and nearly everyone starts with a ring of them. A hopper and a chest feed it."
	]
	quest.5D6EDAE61726AC52.title: "Manasteel Kit"
	quest.5D6EDAE61726AC52.quest_subtitle: "Tools that repair themselves"
	quest.5D6EDAE61726AC52.quest_desc: [
		"&6Manasteel&r tools and armour draw on any mana you carry to fix themselves, so they"
		"effectively never wear out. Without a Mana Tablet in your inventory they are iron"
		"with better durability and enchantability."
	]
	quest.3512AE7B553E3322.title: "Manasteel"
	quest.3512AE7B553E3322.quest_subtitle: "Iron, dunked in mana"
	quest.3512AE7B553E3322.quest_desc: [
		"Drop an iron ingot into a charged &6Mana Pool&r and it comes out as &6Manasteel&r."
		"The same works for a diamond and for a pearl."
	]
	quest.2A28AF533236E628.title: "Mana in Your Pocket"
	quest.2A28AF533236E628.quest_subtitle: "Band and Mirror"
	quest.2A28AF533236E628.quest_desc: [
		"Carry a charge in a Curios slot with a &6Band of Mana&r. A &6Mana Mirror&r, once you have"
		"terrasteel, binds to a pool and draws from it wherever you are."
	]
	quest.024E33A1475E1E54.title: "Pearls and Diamonds"
	quest.024E33A1475E1E54.quest_subtitle: "The two expensive infusions"
	quest.024E33A1475E1E54.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Mana Pearl&r and a &6Mana Diamond&r are the next two things the pool makes, and"
		"both are gates rather than tools. The Runic Altar wants the pearl, so make that first."
	]
	quest.2A7E22788F6A99DA.title: "The Runic Altar"
	quest.2A7E22788F6A99DA.quest_subtitle: "Livingrock and a mana pearl"
	quest.2A7E22788F6A99DA.quest_desc: [
		"Throw ingredients onto the &6Runic Altar&r, add mana, and it returns a &6Rune&r. There"
		"are sixteen, and almost everything later needs one."
		""
		"&7Runes used in the altar's own recipes are returned, not consumed.&r"
	]
	quest.4143F1258BB76BDE.title: "The Four Elements"
	quest.4143F1258BB76BDE.quest_subtitle: "Earth, water, fire, air"
	quest.4143F1258BB76BDE.quest_desc: [
		"The first four runes are made from ordinary things, stone, a fishing rod, nether wart"
		"and a feather, and they gate the twelve after them. Each craft returns two; recipes"
		"pull them constantly."
	]
	quest.6A592BA658BA8AB8.title: "Terra Blade"
	quest.6A592BA658BA8AB8.quest_subtitle: "The end of the flower"
	quest.6A592BA658BA8AB8.quest_desc: [
		"Terrasteel around a livingwood stick. It sometimes throws its swing at range, drinks"
		"your mana to repair itself, and the pick and axe from the same metal are just as good."
	]
	quest.5954FCCE1A59FE20.title: "The Gaia Guardian"
	quest.5954FCCE1A59FE20.quest_subtitle: "Three pylons and a beacon"
	quest.5954FCCE1A59FE20.quest_desc: [
		"Set three &6Gaia Pylons&r around a beacon, throw in a terrasteel ingot, and fight what"
		"turns up. It drops &6Gaia Spirit&r."
		""
		"&7Arena rules apply: a fixed floor size, and it heals if you leave.&r"
	]
	quest.40EDF0B27DEA9437.title: "The Terra Plate"
	quest.40EDF0B27DEA9437.quest_subtitle: "Terrasteel"
	quest.40EDF0B27DEA9437.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Terrestrial Agglomeration Plate&r takes manasteel, a mana pearl, a mana diamond"
		"and an enormous amount of mana, and returns &6Terrasteel&r."
		""
		"&7The plate itself needs the four elemental runes and a Rune of Mana, so build the"
		"altar first. Feed it from several pools at once or it takes all afternoon.&r"
	]
	quest.60B046B183350261.title: "The Elven Gateway"
	quest.60B046B183350261.quest_subtitle: "Alfheim, sort of"
	quest.60B046B183350261.quest_desc: [
		"A frame of livingwood with a &6Gateway Core&r, opened by throwing a terrasteel ingot"
		"at it. Trade through it for &6Elementium&r, &6Dragonstone&r and &6Pixie Dust&r."
		""
		"&7The portal is a shop counter, not a door. You do not go through.&r"
	]
	quest.4CA56727D90C5CAC.title: "Sparks"
	quest.4CA56727D90C5CAC.quest_subtitle: "Mana without line of sight"
	quest.4CA56727D90C5CAC.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &6Spark&r on a pool and another on a mana-using block and mana moves between"
		"them with no spreader beam to line up. Augments change what a spark does: dominant,"
		"recessive, dispersive."
	]
	quest.1D61E38F399710B3.title: "Elven Spreaders"
	quest.1D61E38F399710B3.quest_subtitle: "Faster, further"
	quest.1D61E38F399710B3.quest_desc: [
		"Elementium and dreamwood make a spreader that throws harder than the livingwood"
		"one, which matters once the terra plate is running. Gaia spreaders go faster still."
	]
	quest.25060B61FE4F4322.title: "Manaweave"
	quest.25060B61FE4F4322.quest_subtitle: "Cloth from mana"
	quest.25060B61FE4F4322.quest_desc: [
		"&6Manaweave Cloth&r is spun from mana string and goes into the mod's lightest armour"
		"and several of its stranger relics. It is a component rather than a chestplate."
	]
	chapter.2FEAB12570711519.title: "Botania"
	chapter.2FEAB12570711519.chapter_subtitle: ["Petals, mana and a very long ladder of flowers."]
	quest.6EC93DC95E6D19C4.title: "A Knife and a Reason"
	quest.6EC93DC95E6D19C4.quest_subtitle: "The Sacrificial Knife"
	quest.6EC93DC95E6D19C4.quest_desc: [
		"Blood Magic runs on &6Life Essence&r, and the first source of it is you. A"
		"&6Sacrificial Knife&r used on yourself near an altar fills it."
		""
		"The mod has two halves and this page keeps them apart: the altar and its orbs along"
		"the upper track, demon will and the forge along the lower. The rituals come off the"
		"altar track."
		""
		"&7Mobs are the better source later. A Dagger of Sacrifice handles those.&r"
	]
	quest.459EB8B1547AF4A4.title: "Blank Slates"
	quest.459EB8B1547AF4A4.quest_subtitle: "The altar's first job"
	quest.459EB8B1547AF4A4.quest_desc: [
		"Put stone on the altar and it comes back as a &6Blank Slate&r. Every tier above,"
		"reinforced, imbued, demonic, ethereal, works the same way, and a spare stack of"
		"slates saves a trip back to the altar later."
	]
	quest.42D857D744B777E0.title: "The Blood Altar"
	quest.42D857D744B777E0.quest_subtitle: "Stone, a furnace and gold"
	quest.42D857D744B777E0.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Blood Altar&r holds life essence and transmutes whatever you put on it. Nearly"
		"everything in this chapter passes through here at some point."
		""
		"&7Runes in the ground around it raise its tier, so leave room for them now.&r"
	]
	quest.63C85E779AF88F86.title: "Catch a Soul"
	quest.63C85E779AF88F86.quest_subtitle: "Soul Snares"
	quest.63C85E779AF88F86.quest_desc: [
		"&6Soul Snares&r thrown at a mob make it drop &6Demon Will&r when it dies. Will is the"
		"mod's second resource and has nothing to do with the altar."
		""
		"&7Snares are made on the Blood Altar: the one recipe that crosses from the essence"
		"half of the mod into the will half.&r"
	]
	quest.3AE01BF45B164368.title: "The Weak Blood Orb"
	quest.3AE01BF45B164368.quest_subtitle: "A diamond, given up"
	quest.3AE01BF45B164368.quest_desc: [
		"A diamond on a charged altar becomes a &6Weak Blood Orb&r: a personal reservoir of"
		"life essence, and the key to every recipe after it."
		""
		"&7Bind it by holding right-click. An unbound orb belongs to nobody.&r"
	]
	quest.629E589A65310CC2.title: "The Hellfire Forge"
	quest.629E589A65310CC2.quest_subtitle: "Where will is spent"
	quest.629E589A65310CC2.quest_desc: [
		"Demon will burns out of a &6Tartaric Gem&r in the &6Hellfire Forge&r to craft things the"
		"altar cannot touch. The Petty gem holds little, and it is the one the forge asks for first."
	]
	quest.768E5B7997090AD3.title: "Runes in the Floor"
	quest.768E5B7997090AD3.quest_subtitle: "Tier two and beyond"
	quest.768E5B7997090AD3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Blank Runes&r laid around the altar raise its tier; specialised runes change what"
		"it does, capacity, speed, sacrifice efficiency."
		""
		"&7Tier is checked on the whole structure. One missing rune stalls everything.&r"
	]
	quest.1B441653F0CFDA55.title: "A Fuller Gem"
	quest.1B441653F0CFDA55.quest_subtitle: "The Lesser Tartaric Gem"
	quest.1B441653F0CFDA55.quest_desc: [
		"Each &6Tartaric Gem&r tier holds more will. Filling one is a matter of killing a"
		"great many things with a snare or a soul weapon, and a gem in your inventory"
		"absorbs will on its own."
	]
	quest.16DE2D40F12CD547.title: "The Alchemy Table"
	quest.16DE2D40F12CD547.quest_subtitle: "Recipes the altar cannot do"
	quest.16DE2D40F12CD547.quest_desc: [
		"An orb, some slates and a handful of reagents go into the &6Alchemy Table&r and the"
		"mod's consumables and components come out. Its recipes cost life essence from the"
		"orb, so keep the altar full."
	]
	quest.67C528A63E939124.title: "Soul Tools"
	quest.67C528A63E939124.quest_subtitle: "Weapons that grow with will"
	quest.67C528A63E939124.quest_desc: [
		"Soul tools, the &6Pickaxe&r, &6Axe&r, &6Shovel&r and &6Scythe&r, get stronger the more will"
		"is in the gem you carry, and they collect will as they kill."
	]
	quest.67EFB8CA35BB6051.title: "Sigils"
	quest.67EFB8CA35BB6051.quest_subtitle: "Spend the orb, not the blood"
	quest.67EFB8CA35BB6051.quest_desc: [
		"Read an altar's contents with a &6Divination Sigil&r, and carry five more sigils in one"
		"slot with the &6Sigil of Holding&r. They run off your bound orb rather than your health."
		"Make the Divination Sigil first; working an altar blind is guesswork."
	]
	quest.527437A596B71518.title: "Crystallise It"
	quest.527437A596B71518.quest_subtitle: "The Demon Crystallizer"
	quest.527437A596B71518.quest_desc: [
		"Raw will in the air becomes a growing crystal cluster in a &6Demon Crystallizer&r, one you"
		"can harvest: the farm that replaces snaring mobs by hand."
		""
		"&7A Demon Will Aura Gauge shows how much will is in the chunk.&r"
	]
	quest.6F8806BE51C76924.title: "Apprentice and Magician"
	quest.6F8806BE51C76924.quest_subtitle: "Up the orb ladder"
	quest.6F8806BE51C76924.quest_desc: [
		"Each orb tier holds more and unlocks the recipes above it. The &6Apprentice&r and"
		"&6Magician&r orbs cover most of what this chapter needs; Master and Archmage orbs"
		"exist above them and need tier four and five altars."
	]
	quest.665FCD873E79A46C.title: "The Reaction Chamber"
	quest.665FCD873E79A46C.quest_subtitle: "ARC"
	quest.665FCD873E79A46C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Alchemical Reaction Chamber&r processes ores, fluids and will into the mod's"
		"later components, including &6Blood Shards&r. A tool in its input slot decides"
		"what it does. Its recipe wants a Magician's Blood Orb, so climb the orb ladder first."
	]
	quest.08CCAD22C3F45393.title: "The Master Ritual Stone"
	quest.08CCAD22C3F45393.quest_subtitle: "Where the two halves meet"
	quest.08CCAD22C3F45393.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Master Ritual Stone&r surrounded by plain &6Ritual Stones&r in a pattern. The"
		"pattern decides what the ritual does, and rituals cost life essence from your"
		"bound orb to start and to keep running."
		""
		"&7The stones want a Magician-tier orb, so the altar track has to come first.&r"
	]
	quest.6E1D0A9B61750B89.title: "The Weak Activation Crystal"
	quest.6E1D0A9B61750B89.quest_subtitle: "What lights a ritual"
	quest.6E1D0A9B61750B89.quest_desc: [
		"Made on the altar from a &6Lava Crystal&r. Right-click the master stone with it"
		"and the ritual starts."
		""
		"&7The blood orb does not start rituals. The crystal does.&r"
	]
	quest.40DEBD6FBA51FCDE.title: "The Ritual Diviner"
	quest.40DEBD6FBA51FCDE.quest_subtitle: "Stop placing stones by hand"
	quest.40DEBD6FBA51FCDE.quest_desc: [
		"Stones from your inventory go down in the whole pattern at once with a &6Ritual Diviner&r,"
		"which also tells you which ritual you are looking at. The dusk version handles the"
		"rituals the plain one cannot see."
	]
	quest.1FB18FBA9625308A.title: "A Ritual, Running"
	quest.1FB18FBA9625308A.quest_subtitle: "Pick one and light it"
	quest.1FB18FBA9625308A.quest_desc: [
		"There are dozens: well of suffering, crusher, green grove, magnetism, regeneration."
		"Get one lit and keep it fed. A &6Demon Will Crystal&r harvested from a crystallizer"
		"is the proof that the will half of the mod is running too; the Demon Crystallizer"
		"on the lower track grows them."
		""
		"&7The Well of Suffering over a mob farm is how most altars end up filled.&r"
	]
	quest.781D7D53B07F0570.title: "The Dungeon"
	quest.781D7D53B07F0570.quest_subtitle: "Blood Magic's own dimension"
	quest.781D7D53B07F0570.quest_desc: [
		"The mod keeps a generated dungeon behind a &6Reinforced Resonator&r, full"
		"of the components its late tiers want."
		""
		"&7Everything past the magician orb effectively lives down there.&r"
	]
	quest.6B9C45BD19CE26A4.title: "Incense"
	quest.6B9C45BD19CE26A4.quest_subtitle: "Better sacrifices"
	quest.6B9C45BD19CE26A4.quest_desc: [
		"Paths laid around an &6Incense Altar&r raise how much essence a self-sacrifice yields,"
		"which matters a great deal at higher tiers. Each path tier needs the one before it,"
		"so the paths are built outward."
	]
	quest.62A4328A4F74876A.title: "The Tinkerer"
	quest.62A4328A4F74876A.quest_subtitle: "Reshape a ritual"
	quest.62A4328A4F74876A.quest_desc: [
		"Move a ritual's effect area and change where it points with a &6Ritual Tinkerer&r, so a"
		"ritual can be fitted to a room rather than the other way round."
	]
	chapter.20B7CCA38BFD223C.title: "Blood Magic"
	chapter.20B7CCA38BFD223C.chapter_subtitle: ["An altar that runs on life, a forge that runs on will, and rituals that need both."]
	quest.68D0013EC5A8ECD9.title: "The Worn Notebook"
	quest.68D0013EC5A8ECD9.quest_subtitle: "Read this one first"
	quest.68D0013EC5A8ECD9.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Worn Notebook&r is Ars Nouveau's manual, and new entries appear as you unlock"
		"glyphs. Keeping it open beside you while you write your first spells saves a lot of"
		"guessing."
		""
		"The page splits after the first book: glyphs and casting over the top, source and"
		"how to gather it underneath. The gear and the boss come off the glyph track."
	]
	quest.06277CD5310A7DE1.title: "Archwood"
	quest.06277CD5310A7DE1.quest_subtitle: "Blue, green, red, purple"
	quest.06277CD5310A7DE1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Archwood&r trees grow in magical biomes, and every block in this chapter is made"
		"from their planks and slabs. Any of the four kinds will do; the colour is cosmetic."
	]
	quest.2F66D1C3CA48F357.title: "A Novice's Book"
	quest.2F66D1C3CA48F357.quest_subtitle: "A book and four iron tools"
	quest.2F66D1C3CA48F357.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Novice Spell Book&r holds the spells you write and the source to cast them, and"
		"comes with a handful of glyphs already known. It casts Tier 1 glyphs only; the Mage's"
		"Book unlocks Tier 2."
	]
	quest.4AC6218F212C572F.title: "Source Jars"
	quest.4AC6218F212C572F.quest_subtitle: "Where source is kept"
	quest.4AC6218F212C572F.quest_desc: [
		"Source is stored in a &6Source Jar&r, which hands it to anything nearby that needs some."
		"Everything on this page runs off these, and one jar is a bottleneck almost at once."
	]
	quest.0072C15362B7CA13.title: "Source Gems"
	quest.0072C15362B7CA13.quest_subtitle: "The Imbuement Chamber"
	quest.0072C15362B7CA13.quest_desc: [
		"Lapis becomes &6Source Gems&r in an &6Imbuement Chamber&r, slowly, using source drawn"
		"from the air around it. Source Jars nearby speed it up."
	]
	quest.766602BB999D027A.title: "The Scribe's Table"
	quest.766602BB999D027A.quest_subtitle: "Where glyphs are made"
	quest.766602BB999D027A.quest_desc: [
		"Experience and reagents become &6Glyphs&r at a &6Scribe's Table&r: the verbs and"
		"adjectives you build a spell out of."
		""
		"&7Touch, Projectile and Break get you most of the way on their own.&r"
	]
	quest.67BF042167D0C981.title: "Sourcelinks"
	quest.67BF042167D0C981.quest_subtitle: "Make source out of something else"
	quest.67BF042167D0C981.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Sourcelink&r converts an activity into source. &6Volcanic&r burns fuel, &6Agronomic&r"
		"watches crops grow, &6Vitalic&r feeds on healing, &6Alchemical&r on potions, &6Mycelial&r"
		"on mob kills."
		""
		"&7An Agronomic link beside a colony farm gives the most source for the least effort.&r"
	]
	quest.6971D5E0C5C8C082.title: "Write One"
	quest.6971D5E0C5C8C082.quest_subtitle: "Form, effect, modifier"
	quest.6971D5E0C5C8C082.quest_desc: [
		"Every spell starts with a &6form&r, how it is delivered, then effects, then"
		"modifiers. Projectile, Break, Amplify is a mining laser."
		""
		"&7Spell Parchment copies a spell so you can hand it to somebody else.&r"
	]
	quest.24BEA9F4CDCB2E5D.title: "Relays and Condensers"
	quest.24BEA9F4CDCB2E5D.quest_subtitle: "Moving source around"
	quest.24BEA9F4CDCB2E5D.quest_desc: [
		"Link a &6Source Relay&r with the &6Dominion Wand&r and it carries source between jars"
		"without pipes. The wand links nearly everything in this mod, so make it early."
	]
	quest.3F1529B68849F053.title: "The Enchanting Apparatus"
	quest.3F1529B68849F053.quest_subtitle: "Pedestals in a ring"
	quest.3F1529B68849F053.quest_desc: [
		"An &6Enchanting Apparatus&r with eight &6Arcane Pedestals&r evenly spaced around it is"
		"where most of the mod's real items are made. It draws source from a jar nearby."
	]
	quest.4298CD8A0C3C5B67.title: "Magebloom"
	quest.4298CD8A0C3C5B67.quest_subtitle: "Cloth for the good gear"
	quest.4298CD8A0C3C5B67.quest_desc: [
		"&6Magebloom&r grows from a seed made at the apparatus, and its fibre goes into the"
		"mod's armour and several of its focuses. A Botany Pot farms it happily."
	]
	quest.5EA1DD1BBD8BA4B6.title: "A Mage's Book"
	quest.5EA1DD1BBD8BA4B6.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade the novice"
	quest.5EA1DD1BBD8BA4B6.quest_desc: [
		"Obsidian, three diamonds, two quartz blocks and two blaze rods upgrade the novice book"
		"into the &6Mage's Spell Book&r, which unlocks Tier 2 glyphs and holds more source."
		"Upgrading keeps the spells you already wrote."
	]
	quest.55ED822746ABC119.title: "The Ritual Brazier"
	quest.55ED822746ABC119.quest_subtitle: "Effects that stay on"
	quest.55ED822746ABC119.quest_desc: [
		"Light a &6Ritual Brazier&r with a tablet and it runs that effect over an area: awakening"
		"a tree, growing crops, restoring an area, opening a portal."
		""
		"&7Run Awakening first. The mod's later recipes need what it produces.&r"
	]
	quest.750A666784781561.title: "Enchanter's Gear"
	quest.750A666784781561.quest_subtitle: "Weapons with spells in them"
	quest.750A666784781561.quest_desc: [
		"The apparatus makes an &6Enchanter's Sword&r, &6Bow&r and &6Shield&r, each of which"
		"carries a spell it casts when used. Source has to be flowing by now, so the lower"
		"track matters here even though the wire comes from above."
		""
		"&7The shield casts its spell when it blocks a hit, so give it a self-heal rather"
		"than damage.&r"
	]
	quest.2128BAFDC7730D1E.title: "Summon a Familiar"
	quest.2128BAFDC7730D1E.quest_subtitle: "The Focus of Summoning"
	quest.2128BAFDC7730D1E.quest_desc: [
		"Wear a &6Focus of Summoning&r in your Curios slot and a summon spell produces a permanent"
		"familiar that follows you. You can keep one at a time, so choose it for how you fight."
		""
		"&7The focus itself wants a Wilden Tribute from the Chimera on the row above.&r"
	]
	quest.447E949DA72C9E77.title: "Spell Turrets"
	quest.447E949DA72C9E77.quest_subtitle: "Automation, of a sort"
	quest.447E949DA72C9E77.quest_desc: [
		"On a redstone pulse a &6Spell Turret&r casts its stored spell. Point one at a farm, a"
		"mob spawner or a door; anything you can write, a turret can repeat forever."
	]
	quest.1A0F79465EA37740.title: "Drygmies and Wixies"
	quest.1A0F79465EA37740.quest_subtitle: "Small creatures with jobs"
	quest.1A0F79465EA37740.quest_desc: [
		"Drygmies collect mob drops without killing anything; a &6Wixie&r crafts from a cauldron;"
		"a &6Whirlisprig&r farms."
		""
		"&7A drygmy pen around a few mobs is a drop farm with no killing and no redstone.&r"
	]
	quest.4EC6B27F0AA4478E.title: "The Wilden Chimera"
	quest.4EC6B27F0AA4478E.quest_subtitle: "Ars Nouveau's boss"
	quest.4EC6B27F0AA4478E.quest_desc: [
		"Wilden Stalkers, Hunters and Guardians drop the wings, horns and spikes that summon"
		"the &6Wilden Chimera&r, and the Chimera drops the &6Wilden Tribute&r."
		""
		"&7Fight it somewhere open. It changes what it does when it gets low.&r"
	]
	quest.54B7B4A150366978.title: "Jar of Light"
	quest.54B7B4A150366978.quest_subtitle: "And the rest of the small things"
	quest.54B7B4A150366978.quest_desc: [
		"The apparatus makes a long tail of everyday items: a &6Jar of Light&r, warp scrolls,"
		"potion flasks, amulets. Several of them save real time once source is flowing."
	]
	quest.521A0F23CEDBE551.title: "The Archmage's Book"
	quest.521A0F23CEDBE551.quest_subtitle: "A nether star and a tribute"
	quest.521A0F23CEDBE551.quest_desc: [
		"A nether star, a &6Wilden Tribute&r, two emeralds, three pearls and a totem turn the"
		"Mage's Book into the &6Archmage Spell Book&r, the last of the three."
	]
	quest.4B38603BE11DB129.title: "A Working Tower"
	quest.4B38603BE11DB129.quest_subtitle: "Everything, in one room"
	quest.4B38603BE11DB129.quest_desc: [
		"Sourcelinks feeding jars, jars feeding an apparatus, a brazier running, and a"
		"familiar sat on the stairs."
		""
		"From here the mod is a workshop rather than a set of recipes."
	]
	chapter.585C78CEF680A292.title: "Ars Nouveau"
	chapter.585C78CEF680A292.chapter_subtitle: ["Glyphs, spell books and a source network to pay for them."]
	quest.7544B127A3949536.title: "A Shrine in the Wild"
	quest.7544B127A3949536.quest_subtitle: "Five of them, one per source"
	quest.7544B127A3949536.quest_desc: [
		"&6Earth, Sea, Sky, Sun&r and &6Moon&r each have a small marble shrine somewhere in"
		"the world, with an &6Ancient Font&r at its centre. Find one, take the dust from"
		"under it, then sleep. You wake knowing how to make the &6Mundane Wand&r."
	]
	quest.1635323E0B2CEC80.title: "A Mundane Wand"
	quest.1635323E0B2CEC80.quest_subtitle: "A stick and a pinch of dust"
	quest.1635323E0B2CEC80.quest_desc: [
		"A wooden rod and some &6Essence Dust&r make the &6Mundane Wand&r, which siphons mana"
		"out of a font and spends it again. Right-click a font with the wand held; ten mana"
		"is the first goal."
	]
	quest.647BF74858FFE027.title: "The Grimoire"
	quest.647BF74858FFE027.quest_subtitle: "A wand, a bookshelf, a book"
	quest.647BF74858FFE027.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Grimoire&r is the mod's research tree, guidebook and progress tracker in one."
		"It arrives the moment you wave a &6Mundane Wand&r at a bookshelf, and everything Primal"
		"Magick does is unlocked inside it."
	]
	quest.24E949ECA1BEF1D2.title: "Marble"
	quest.24E949ECA1BEF1D2.quest_subtitle: "The mod builds in stone"
	quest.24E949ECA1BEF1D2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Marble&r makes almost every Primal Magick block, and it generates in blobs"
		"underground like an ore. Enchanted and hallowed marble come later and are not"
		"interchangeable."
	]
	quest.7D30B00ED1E9FF0F.title: "The Arcane Workbench"
	quest.7D30B00ED1E9FF0F.quest_subtitle: "Crafting that costs mana"
	quest.7D30B00ED1E9FF0F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Arcane Workbench&r is never crafted. Wave your wand at an ordinary crafting"
		"table and you are granted it."
		"It takes a wand in its slot and spends mana from it, and nearly every recipe from"
		"here on is an arcane one."
	]
	quest.01736BEECD660A0F.title: "Better Wands"
	quest.01736BEECD660A0F.quest_subtitle: "Core, caps and gem"
	quest.01736BEECD660A0F.quest_desc: [
		"A real wand is assembled from a &6core&r, two &6caps&r and a &6gem&r, and each part"
		"changes how much mana it holds and how efficiently it spends it."
		""
		"&7Heartwood core, iron caps and an apprentice gem make a solid first wand.&r"
	]
	quest.2545793303F2CD80.title: "The Mana Charger"
	quest.2545793303F2CD80.quest_subtitle: "Refilling without a shrine"
	quest.2545793303F2CD80.quest_desc: [
		"Essence pushed into a wand by a &6Mana Charger&r saves the walk to a font every time the"
		"workbench runs dry. It takes essence of whichever source you are short of."
	]
	quest.1DDC9F1CB904BB7C.title: "An Artificial Font"
	quest.1DDC9F1CB904BB7C.quest_subtitle: "Your own mana supply"
	quest.1DDC9F1CB904BB7C.quest_desc: [
		"Mana of one source regenerates at your own base from an &6Artificial Font&r. There is"
		"one per source, so plan a room for five now and four more later."
	]
	quest.0F44CC77C072BEA7.title: "Look Closer"
	quest.0F44CC77C072BEA7.quest_subtitle: "Magnifying glass and analysis"
	quest.0F44CC77C072BEA7.quest_desc: [
		"Analyse an item with a &6Magnifying Glass&r and the Grimoire learns what it is made of."
		"An &6Analysis Table&r does it in bulk. One of each type of thing is enough; a second"
		"stone teaches nothing."
	]
	quest.46CB7D5A5274CA60.title: "Spellcraft"
	quest.46CB7D5A5274CA60.quest_subtitle: "Write your own spells"
	quest.46CB7D5A5274CA60.quest_desc: [
		"Spells are built at a &6Spellcrafting Altar&r on a &6Blank Spell Scroll&r out of a"
		"vehicle, a payload and modifiers, then bound to a wand."
		""
		"&7Cost scales sharply with power. Cheap spells get cast many times more often.&r"
	]
	quest.61110A685486DD96.title: "Essence"
	quest.61110A685486DD96.quest_subtitle: "Dust, shard, crystal, cluster"
	quest.61110A685486DD96.quest_desc: [
		"Every source has four grades of &6Essence&r, and combining four of one grade makes"
		"one of the next."
		""
		"&7A Calcinator burns ordinary blocks down into essence, and is worth building early.&r"
	]
	quest.514A3EDD75B04C1B.title: "Blood, Infernal, Void"
	quest.514A3EDD75B04C1B.quest_subtitle: "The three forbidden sources"
	quest.514A3EDD75B04C1B.quest_desc: [
		"Past the five primal sources sit three more, unlocked by research the Grimoire"
		"marks as forbidden."
		""
		"&7The pack's summoning altar runs on blood essence, so this branch matters well"
		"beyond this mod.&r"
	]
	quest.2E74FD6EF0B10A48.title: "Runework"
	quest.2E74FD6EF0B10A48.quest_subtitle: "Carving and scribing"
	quest.2E74FD6EF0B10A48.quest_desc: [
		"Runes cut from marble at a &6Runecarving Table&r go onto gear at a &6Runescribing Altar&r"
		"as the mod's own permanent enchantments, which stack with vanilla ones."
	]
	quest.6B19D2B0A43E5792.title: "The Sanguine Crucible"
	quest.6B19D2B0A43E5792.quest_subtitle: "Blood magick, this mod's version"
	quest.6B19D2B0A43E5792.quest_desc: [
		"Life goes into a &6Sanguine Crucible&r and blood essence comes out, which fuels the"
		"forbidden half of the tree. It has nothing to do with the Blood Magic chapter, despite the name."
	]
	quest.2A1CF4035E3E5BCE.title: "Alchemy"
	quest.2A1CF4035E3E5BCE.quest_subtitle: "The Concocter"
	quest.2A1CF4035E3E5BCE.quest_desc: [
		"Potions and &6Ambrosia&r are brewed in a &6Concocter&r. Ambrosia grants attunement to a"
		"source rather than a status effect, and attunement unlocks the later halves of the"
		"research tree."
	]
	quest.48982F0B1A6F04AF.title: "The Infernal Furnace"
	quest.48982F0B1A6F04AF.quest_subtitle: "Smelting, forbidden"
	quest.48982F0B1A6F04AF.quest_desc: [
		"Smelting runs many times faster in an &6Infernal Furnace&r and pays for it in infernal"
		"essence. Hexium and Hallowsteel are made past this point."
	]
	quest.202F2F50231DA476.title: "The Ritual Altar"
	quest.202F2F50231DA476.quest_subtitle: "Big work needs a room"
	quest.202F2F50231DA476.quest_desc: [
		"Props placed around a &6Ritual Altar&r, bloodletters, celestial harps, incense braziers,"
		"let it perform the mod's largest recipes."
		""
		"&7A ritual fails if a prop is wrong or too far away. The Grimoire lists the layout.&r"
	]
	quest.18174F898ECF4918.title: "Hallowed"
	quest.18174F898ECF4918.quest_subtitle: "The ninth source"
	quest.18174F898ECF4918.quest_desc: [
		"&6Hallowed&r essence sits above all eight and is the hardest thing in the mod to"
		"produce at any scale. Hallowsteel wand caps are the reason to bother."
	]
	quest.75C065F245C6F9F5.title: "An Archmage's Wand"
	quest.75C065F245C6F9F5.quest_subtitle: "The best parts you can assemble"
	quest.75C065F245C6F9F5.quest_desc: [
		"An &6Archmage Gem&r set in the best core and caps you can assemble, with nothing above"
		"it. Each part is a separate research entry, so this is a long project."
	]
	quest.028D953A1A7FD12C.title: "The Whole Tree"
	quest.028D953A1A7FD12C.quest_subtitle: "Nine sources, all of them read"
	quest.028D953A1A7FD12C.quest_desc: [
		"Every source attuned, every discipline opened, and a Grimoire with no grey entries"
		"left in it."
		""
		"&7Every entry above must be researched before the Grimoire clears. Expect this to"
		"take longer than any other chapter.&r"
	]
	chapter.1D21A70AB9E008B9.title: "Primal Magick"
	chapter.1D21A70AB9E008B9.chapter_subtitle: ["Earth, Sea, Sky, Sun and Moon — and three more the Grimoire marks as forbidden."]
	quest.3CE4EE4B21CEC15B.title: "Arcane Essence"
	quest.3CE4EE4B21CEC15B.quest_subtitle: "The mod's one ingredient"
	quest.3CE4EE4B21CEC15B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Arcane Essence&r is looted from the mod's towers and magical chests, and almost"
		"everything here is built out of it. &6Arcane Debris&r in the deepslate layer is the"
		"mithril route."
		""
		"&7The book and its tools run along the top of this page, four school pages hang off"
		"them, and the towers and their loot sit below.&r"
	]
	quest.0866CE340C54E9D3.title: "An Ironbound Tome"
	quest.0866CE340C54E9D3.quest_subtitle: "Chain, leather and paper"
	quest.0866CE340C54E9D3.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Spell Book&r holds spells and the mana to cast them. The copper Flimsy Journal is"
		"the cheapest; iron, gold and diamond books hold more."
		""
		"&7It is held in the offhand and cast with the keybind, not by right-clicking.&r"
	]
	quest.5D30681BF8000FE4.title: "The Inscription Table"
	quest.5D30681BF8000FE4.quest_subtitle: "Put a spell in the book"
	quest.5D30681BF8000FE4.quest_desc: [
		"Move a spell off a scroll and into a book slot at an &6Inscription Table&r. Scrolls"
		"come from loot, from the mod's towers, and from ink. A scroll is consumed, so choose"
		"the slot before you commit."
	]
	quest.6FC7B0C00C0087E9.title: "Ink and Cauldron"
	quest.6FC7B0C00C0087E9.quest_subtitle: "Make your own scrolls"
	quest.6FC7B0C00C0087E9.quest_desc: [
		"Ink comes out of an &6Alchemist Cauldron&r in five grades, and better ink writes"
		"higher-level spells onto a blank scroll."
		""
		"&7The same cauldron brews elixirs, which stack with vanilla potion effects.&r"
	]
	quest.54554D09EFE7221B.title: "The Arcane Anvil"
	quest.54554D09EFE7221B.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade what you have"
	quest.54554D09EFE7221B.quest_desc: [
		"Apply &6Upgrade Orbs&r and &6Runes&r to gear at an &6Arcane Anvil&r: more mana, shorter"
		"cooldowns, a stronger school affinity. Each item takes a limited number, so plan the set."
	]
	quest.67BF8F82AB765F98.title: "The Wayward Compass"
	quest.67BF8F82AB765F98.quest_subtitle: "Find the towers"
	quest.67BF8F82AB765F98.quest_desc: [
		"Point a &6Wayward Compass&r and it finds the mod's structures: pyromancer tower, evoker"
		"fort, ice spider den, ancient battleground, citadel."
		""
		"&7Furled maps do the same for specific ones, if you find them first.&r"
	]
	quest.5BD129D2C787DDBC.title: "The Citadel"
	quest.5BD129D2C787DDBC.quest_subtitle: "Where the good scrolls are"
	quest.5BD129D2C787DDBC.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Citadel&r is the mod's largest structure and the reliable source of legendary"
		"ink, upgrade orbs and the higher-tier scrolls. It is heavily defended, so bring a"
		"school you have upgraded."
	]
	quest.227E8B8809D08D5E.title: "A Pocket to Keep"
	quest.227E8B8809D08D5E.quest_subtitle: "Iron's own dimension"
	quest.227E8B8809D08D5E.quest_desc: [
		"Cast the &6Pocket Dimension&r spell, an Ender school spell, and you land in a small"
		"private space: somewhere quiet to store things and practise spells away from anything"
		"you have built."
	]
	quest.39FCDB9302C87832.title: "Pyromancer's Robes"
	quest.39FCDB9302C87832.quest_subtitle: "Armour with a school on it"
	quest.39FCDB9302C87832.quest_desc: [
		"Each school has a full armour set that lowers its spells' cost and raises their"
		"power, made by combining plain Wizard Robes with that school's rune. Mixing sets is usually worse than"
		"committing to one."
	]
	quest.33D0C00E14243365.title: "Fire"
	quest.33D0C00E14243365.quest_subtitle: "The straightforward damage school"
	quest.33D0C00E14243365.quest_desc: [
		"Burning hands, fireballs, blaze storms. Fire is the plainest damage school, and it"
		"has a tower of its own to raid. Fire Runes are eight blaze rods around a blank"
		"runestone; the Pyromancer Tower is where the Upgrade Orbs are."
	]
	quest.430AE8D133443E1A.title: "The Dead King"
	quest.430AE8D133443E1A.quest_subtitle: "Eldritch, and a phylactery"
	quest.430AE8D133443E1A.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Eldritch&r school comes off the mod's own boss, and its manuscript and"
		"phylactery are the last things it has to give."
		""
		"&7Eldritch spells are the strongest in the mod and cost the most to cast.&r"
	]
	quest.7F0936928FAD14DF.title: "An Archevoker's Set"
	quest.7F0936928FAD14DF.quest_subtitle: "The top of the armour tree"
	quest.7F0936928FAD14DF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Archevoker&r plate, upgraded on the arcane anvil with every orb you collected on"
		"the way here. Upgrade slots are finite, which means deciding what the build is"
		"before the first orb goes on."
	]
	quest.62ABA628305294D2.title: "Ice"
	quest.62ABA628305294D2.quest_subtitle: "Slow them, freeze them, shatter them"
	quest.62ABA628305294D2.quest_desc: [
		"Frost, cones of cold, and an ice block you can put a boss inside for a few seconds."
		"The Ice Spider Den is where the cryomancer gear lives."
	]
	quest.6DB0B904FBB6102B.title: "Staves and Blades"
	quest.6DB0B904FBB6102B.quest_subtitle: "Focus items"
	quest.6DB0B904FBB6102B.quest_desc: [
		"An &6Ice Staff&r, a &6Boreal Blade&r, a &6Hellrazor&r: weapons that cast a spell of"
		"their own on top of hitting things. A staff in the main hand and a book in the"
		"offhand is the standard build."
	]
	quest.0025AC023FCC224E.title: "A Full Spell Book"
	quest.0025AC023FCC224E.quest_subtitle: "Every slot written"
	quest.0025AC023FCC224E.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Dragonskin&r or diamond book with every slot filled by a spell you chose, on a"
		"set of armour that makes them cheap."
		""
		"&7Slot count is fixed by the book tier, so fill the last slots with utility spells"
		"rather than a second damage school.&r"
	]
	quest.24615257F9F60A8E.title: "Rings and Amulets"
	quest.24615257F9F60A8E.quest_subtitle: "Curios for casters"
	quest.24615257F9F60A8E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ring of Recovery&r, &6Ring of Expediency&r and the affinity rings, plus amulets that"
		"raise concentration, all in Curios slots. Cooldown reduction makes the biggest"
		"difference in a fight."
	]
	quest.2707EA92E29594C9.title: "Holy and Blood"
	quest.2707EA92E29594C9.quest_subtitle: "Two opposite schools"
	quest.2707EA92E29594C9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Holy&r heals and shields; &6Blood&r spends your own health to skip the mana cost."
		"They are not meant to be taken together, and Holy is the closest thing this pack"
		"has to a support class."
	]
	quest.2882C0493465DFDC.title: "Ender and Evocation"
	quest.2882C0493465DFDC.quest_subtitle: "Teleports and summons"
	quest.2882C0493465DFDC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ender&r moves you around the battlefield; &6Evocation&r fills it with summoned help"
		"that fights on your behalf."
		""
		"&7A Conjurer's Talisman raises how many summons you can keep at once.&r"
	]
	quest.3991AE17DCE7785B.title: "Elixirs"
	quest.3991AE17DCE7785B.quest_subtitle: "From the same cauldron"
	quest.3991AE17DCE7785B.quest_desc: [
		"The cauldron brews &6Evasion&r, &6Oakskin&r, &6Invisibility&r and healing elixirs, in"
		"ordinary and greater grades. A stack of Greater Healing is the one to keep on you."
	]
	chapter.0993C72408188148.title: "Iron's Spells"
	chapter.0993C72408188148.chapter_subtitle: ["Ten schools of magic, a book to hold them, and an anvil to improve them."]
	quest.4040B33EE21FC4A2.title: "The Dictionary of Spirits"
	quest.4040B33EE21FC4A2.quest_subtitle: "Read before drawing anything"
	quest.4040B33EE21FC4A2.quest_desc: [
		"Occultism's guidebook is the only place the ritual diagrams are written down, and"
		"every circle in the mod is in it. It is made from a book and a Demon's Dream seed."
		""
		"&7Three branches leave the first summon: bound spirits and their sight above,"
		"familiars and the spirit ladder in the middle, the pack's altar and its summons below.&r"
	]
	quest.70D3AD919239E224.title: "Chalk"
	quest.70D3AD919239E224.quest_subtitle: "White first, then gold"
	quest.70D3AD919239E224.quest_desc: [
		"Circles are drawn with &6Chalk&r. White is the cheap one; gold, purple and red mark"
		"the bigger rituals, and impure chalk is the halfway step that needs purifying."
	]
	quest.05B42EA935F60186.title: "Bowls in the Circle"
	quest.05B42EA935F60186.quest_subtitle: "Sacrificial and golden"
	quest.05B42EA935F60186.quest_desc: [
		"A ritual is a chalk circle, a &6Golden Sacrificial Bowl&r at the centre and plain"
		"&6Sacrificial Bowls&r around it holding the ingredients. Four bowls to start; the"
		"later rituals want eight and a bigger circle."
	]
	quest.0DC9D1BBA2D2D242.title: "A Book of Binding"
	quest.0DC9D1BBA2D2D242.quest_subtitle: "Naming what you are calling"
	quest.0DC9D1BBA2D2D242.quest_desc: [
		"Name an &6Empty Book of Binding&r, Foliot, Djinni, Afrit or Marid, and that decides"
		"which spirit the circle can hold. Foliot is the weakest and the one everything starts"
		"with."
	]
	quest.52A7E124C052807B.title: "Spirits With Jobs"
	quest.52A7E124C052807B.quest_subtitle: "Books of Calling"
	quest.52A7E124C052807B.quest_desc: [
		"Assign a bound spirit to work with a &6Book of Calling&r: a lumberjack that fells trees,"
		"a cleaner that tidies chests, a porter that moves items. They keep working while you"
		"are elsewhere, which is the point of binding them."
	]
	quest.601C4CDC9011661E.title: "Summon a Foliot"
	quest.601C4CDC9011661E.quest_subtitle: "The first spirit"
	quest.601C4CDC9011661E.quest_desc: [
		"Draw the circle, fill the bowls, light the candle and read the book. The spirit"
		"that turns up goes into a &6Magic Lamp&r or straight into a job."
		""
		"&7A ritual takes a while and can be interrupted, which is why it is done somewhere quiet.&r"
	]
	quest.36E9C33A21468621.title: "The Summoning Altar"
	quest.36E9C33A21468621.quest_subtitle: "Rewritten for this pack"
	quest.36E9C33A21468621.quest_desc: [
		"AK3 changes this recipe. Two &6Candles&r and a &6Wither Skeleton Skull&r on top,"
		"&6Yellow Wool&r either side of &6Red Wool&r in the middle, and three &6Spruce Planks&r"
		"along the bottom."
		""
		"&7JEI shows the pack's version, not the mod's default.&r"
	]
	quest.3B1DB1AB92634593.title: "Otherworld Sight"
	quest.3B1DB1AB92634593.quest_subtitle: "Goggles and the divination rod"
	quest.3B1DB1AB92634593.quest_desc: [
		"&6Otherworld Goggles&r reveal blocks that are not there without them, and a"
		"&6Divination Rod&r points at ore through stone."
		""
		"&7Demon's Dream fruit gives the same sight for a minute, far more cheaply.&r"
	]
	quest.096D9E4D8261FE56.title: "Blood Crystals"
	quest.096D9E4D8261FE56.quest_subtitle: "The altar's usual catalyst"
	quest.096D9E4D8261FE56.quest_desc: [
		"Nearly every summon this pack wrote uses a Primal Magick &6Blood Crystal&r as its"
		"catalyst, placed on the altar with the ingredients around it. Primal Magick's"
		"forbidden research therefore gates this whole branch."
	]
	quest.30A569429F56DF0E.title: "Djinni and Afrit"
	quest.30A569429F56DF0E.quest_subtitle: "Up the spirit ladder"
	quest.30A569429F56DF0E.quest_desc: [
		"Each tier of spirit does more and demands a larger circle and rarer ingredients."
		"&6Djinni&r manage machines; &6Afrit&r mine the deep. Purple chalk for djinni, red"
		"for afrit."
	]
	quest.7213E006ED48BC94.title: "Iesnium"
	quest.7213E006ED48BC94.quest_subtitle: "A metal only spirits can see"
	quest.7213E006ED48BC94.quest_desc: [
		"&6Iesnium&r ore exists in the Nether only while you wear the goggles, and it is what"
		"the mod's late blocks are built from. The goggles and a pickaxe are all the trip needs."
	]
	quest.7D1DD61054C11EFA.title: "Call Something Small"
	quest.7D1DD61054C11EFA.quest_subtitle: "A pig, and then a Draugr"
	quest.7D1DD61054C11EFA.quest_desc: [
		"A Blood Crystal on the altar with three live chickens standing in its area returns a pig, the"
		"test run. A bone block and rotten flesh with a pig sacrificed call a &6Draugr&r."
		""
		"&7Every recipe here needs a live sacrifice standing in the altar's area.&r"
	]
	quest.11263387FEF6B44B.title: "Familiars"
	quest.11263387FEF6B44B.quest_subtitle: "Something small on your shoulder"
	quest.11263387FEF6B44B.quest_desc: [
		"Occultism's familiar rituals produce a long list of small companions, a bat, a"
		"beaver, a devil, a dragon, a beholder, each with its own trick. Most want a Djinni"
		"circle; only the beaver, deer, parrot, blacksmith and greedy come off a Foliot one."
		""
		"&7A Familiar Ring lets you carry one and swap it out. The ring itself costs a Soul Gem.&r"
	]
	quest.7B7C40CD67D6A6CA.title: "Storage Actuators"
	quest.7B7C40CD67D6A6CA.quest_subtitle: "Occultism's answer to a warehouse"
	quest.7B7C40CD67D6A6CA.quest_desc: [
		"Storage that a bound spirit fetches from is a &6Dimensional Matrix&r with a stabiliser"
		"and an actuator. It needs no power and no cables; it costs spirits instead, and the"
		"matrix itself is a Djinni ritual, so bind one first."
	]
	quest.48740E7892E85EED.title: "Call Something Large"
	quest.48740E7892E85EED.quest_subtitle: "The Harbinger and the Ancient Remnant"
	quest.48740E7892E85EED.quest_desc: [
		"&6Three Wither Skeleton Skulls&r and a pig fetch the &6Harbinger&r. &6Sixteen Bone"
		"Blocks&r and a gold ingot fetch the &6Ancient Remnant&r. Cheaper than finding their"
		"arenas, and you still have to win the fight."
	]
	quest.1F990B50E582132E.title: "Bind a Marid"
	quest.1F990B50E582132E.quest_subtitle: "The last spirit"
	quest.1F990B50E582132E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Marid&r is the top of Occultism, a master miner and the most expensive circle"
		"the mod draws. It needs iesnium and emerald blocks, diamond and a ghast tear."
	]
	quest.7D5FC4D5F43F8C29.title: "Skreecher and Soul"
	quest.7D5FC4D5F43F8C29.quest_subtitle: "A summon from Alex's Mobs"
	quest.7D5FC4D5F43F8C29.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Sculk&r catalyst with three sculk veins and a fermented spider eye calls an"
		"Alex's Mobs &6Skreecher&r. Its soul is a component in the last recipe this pack"
		"wrote, and this is the only summon here that wants no blood crystal."
	]
	quest.551B21729E028CCB.title: "Everything Answering"
	quest.551B21729E028CCB.quest_subtitle: "A circle for every job"
	quest.551B21729E028CCB.quest_desc: [
		"Spirits mining, spirits carrying, a familiar on your shoulder and an altar in the"
		"corner that fetches bosses on request."
		""
		"&7A Soul Gem stores a live mob so you can move it anywhere.&r"
	]
	quest.42BE9028AB0597A8.title: "Open a Gateway"
	quest.42BE9028AB0597A8.quest_subtitle: "The pack's own last recipe"
	quest.42BE9028AB0597A8.quest_desc: [
		"A bone helmet as catalyst, sixty-four blood essence dust, sixty-four necrotic bones,"
		"a wither chestplate, a blood crystal and a skreecher soul. It returns a &6Gate"
		"Pearl&r for the Iudex gateway."
		""
		"&7JEI does not list this. It is written in the pack's own scripts.&r"
	]
	chapter.2C10191A26D5AF1B.title: "The Summoning Circle"
	chapter.2C10191A26D5AF1B.chapter_subtitle: ["Chalk, lamps and familiars — and an altar this pack rewrote itself."]
	quest.6340CA22FC845EFF.title: "Andesite Alloy"
	quest.6340CA22FC845EFF.quest_subtitle: "Andesite and an iron nugget"
	quest.6340CA22FC845EFF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Andesite Alloy&r is Create's first material and goes into almost every block it"
		"has, so make it by the stack. A mixer over a basin makes it much faster later."
		""
		"&7The page runs andesite first, brass second: millstone and press before brass, belts"
		"and boilers off the casing, and the crushing wheels once the crafters exist.&r"
	]
	quest.0960883513DB669C.title: "Shafts and Cogs"
	quest.0960883513DB669C.quest_subtitle: "How power moves"
	quest.0960883513DB669C.quest_desc: [
		"Rotation travels in a line along a &6Shaft&r, turns a corner at a &6Cogwheel&r, and"
		"changes speed where a &6Large Cogwheel&r meets a small one."
		""
		"&7Speed and stress are two different budgets, and both run out.&r"
	]
	quest.140BD92BAEBE48F4.title: "Wheel or Windmill"
	quest.140BD92BAEBE48F4.quest_subtitle: "Water wheel or windmill"
	quest.140BD92BAEBE48F4.quest_desc: [
		"Either a &6Water Wheel&r in flowing water or a &6Windmill Bearing&r with sails on it. Both"
		"are free forever once built; the wheel is the one this quest checks for."
	]
	quest.3F9B030C11322144.title: "A Factory That Runs"
	quest.3F9B030C11322144.quest_subtitle: "Everything, connected"
	quest.3F9B030C11322144.quest_desc: [
		"Water wheels driving a crafter ring, a sequenced-assembly line making mechanisms, and"
		"a train that takes the output somewhere useful."
		""
		"&7The alternator turns rotation into FE and the motor turns it back. This is how"
		"Create powers an AE2 network.&r"
	]
	quest.4465E88E9523C23A.title: "Belts and Funnels"
	quest.4465E88E9523C23A.quest_subtitle: "Moving items about"
	quest.4465E88E9523C23A.quest_desc: [
		"Items ride a &6Mechanical Belt&r between two shafts; &6Funnels&r load and unload it;"
		"&6Chutes&r do the same vertically."
		""
		"&7A belt runs between two shafts that are level, or that rise exactly one block for"
		"every block of run.&r"
	]
	quest.125DFFF0D0162DE3.title: "Andesite Casing"
	quest.125DFFF0D0162DE3.quest_subtitle: "What machines are wrapped in"
	quest.125DFFF0D0162DE3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Andesite Casing&r is stripped logs and andesite alloy, the shell of every early"
		"machine in the mod. Casing on a shaft also stops things connecting to it by accident."
	]
	quest.1FE156BAA13020EA.title: "Trains"
	quest.1FE156BAA13020EA.quest_subtitle: "A railway you actually build"
	quest.1FE156BAA13020EA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Track&r, a &6Station&r, a &6Train Casing&r and a schedule, and Create's trains run"
		"themselves across whatever you lay. Hold the track item, click one rail then another,"
		"and it fills the curve in between from your stack."
	]
	quest.274B1BCBF2371BF8.title: "The Blaze Burner"
	quest.274B1BCBF2371BF8.quest_subtitle: "Heat for the basin"
	quest.274B1BCBF2371BF8.quest_desc: [
		"Catch a blaze in an &6Empty Blaze Burner&r. Feed it fuel for heat, or a &6Blaze Cake&r"
		"for superheat, which is a separate tier of recipe rather than a faster one."
	]
	quest.174DE339EBF0ADA7.title: "The Millstone"
	quest.174DE339EBF0ADA7.quest_subtitle: "Grinding, cheaply"
	quest.174DE339EBF0ADA7.quest_desc: [
		"Drop something into a &6Millstone&r with a cogwheel underneath and it grinds: ore to"
		"dust, wheat to flour, bone to meal. It is slow, costs almost nothing, and works from"
		"the first water wheel."
	]
	quest.60F24B5741CD6F7A.title: "Contraptions"
	quest.60F24B5741CD6F7A.quest_subtitle: "Blocks that move together"
	quest.60F24B5741CD6F7A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pistons&r, &6Bearings&r, &6Gantries&r and &6Pulleys&r pick up a structure and move it."
		"Add drills and saws and it mines as it goes. Super Glue and Chassis decide what"
		"comes along and what stays."
	]
	quest.667C874F4D178EEF.title: "Fluids"
	quest.667C874F4D178EEF.quest_subtitle: "Pipes, pumps and tanks"
	quest.667C874F4D178EEF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fluid Pipes&r driven by a &6Mechanical Pump&r fill &6Fluid Tanks&r, and a &6Spout&r pours"
		"the contents onto items on a belt. A pipe with no pump does nothing at all."
	]
	quest.3D1B2CAA040E4D20.title: "Press and Basin"
	quest.3D1B2CAA040E4D20.quest_subtitle: "Plates and mixing"
	quest.3D1B2CAA040E4D20.quest_desc: [
		"Plates come from a &6Mechanical Press&r over a depot; a &6Basin&r under a &6Mechanical"
		"Mixer&r combines things, hot or cold."
		""
		"&7A blaze burner under the basin unlocks half the recipe list.&r"
	]
	quest.7BFC800BBC981BB4.title: "Sequenced Assembly"
	quest.7BFC800BBC981BB4.quest_subtitle: "Recipes with steps"
	quest.7BFC800BBC981BB4.quest_desc: [
		"Nobody crafts a &6Precision Mechanism&r. It is built on a depot by a line of deployers"
		"and presses, one step at a time."
		""
		"&7Every step has a failure chance, which is the argument for building the line"
		"rather than doing it by hand.&r"
	]
	quest.7D8E1C1B333F290C.title: "Schematics"
	quest.7D8E1C1B333F290C.quest_subtitle: "Build it twice"
	quest.7D8E1C1B333F290C.quest_desc: [
		"Record a build with a &6Schematic and Quill&r and a &6Schematicannon&r fires it back out"
		"somewhere else, from a chest of materials, burning gunpowder as it goes."
		""
		"&7It will copy a colony building block for block.&r"
	]
	quest.4DEEE0DABE9CDC52.title: "Zinc and Brass"
	quest.4DEEE0DABE9CDC52.quest_subtitle: "The second tier"
	quest.4DEEE0DABE9CDC52.quest_desc: [
		"&6Zinc&r ore plus copper, mixed over a heater, makes &6Brass&r, and brass is the gate"
		"on everything clever Create does."
		""
		"&7A Blaze Burner fed with blaze cake is the heater you want.&r"
	]
	quest.2F0520EC28534C76.title: "Electron Tubes"
	quest.2F0520EC28534C76.quest_subtitle: "Brass, in useful form"
	quest.2F0520EC28534C76.quest_desc: [
		"Polished rose quartz and an iron sheet make an &6Electron Tube&r, and the smart machines are built"
		"from it. Rose quartz is quartz crafted with redstone dust, then polished with sandpaper."
	]
	quest.2301A6E5B2C75279.title: "Mechanical Crafters"
	quest.2301A6E5B2C75279.quest_subtitle: "Automated crafting, Create's way"
	quest.2301A6E5B2C75279.quest_desc: [
		"A ring of &6Mechanical Crafters&r pointed at each other assembles a recipe and spits"
		"out the result. Crushing Wheels are made this way, and so is nearly everything expensive."
	]
	quest.4FAE5882885980B6.title: "Steam and Boilers"
	quest.4FAE5882885980B6.quest_subtitle: "More stress than a water wheel"
	quest.4FAE5882885980B6.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &6Steam Engine&r on a boiler and it produces many times the stress of a water"
		"wheel, scaling with how many tanks the boiler has. Boilers want water and heat, both"
		"of which are easier once fluids are running."
	]
	quest.4D980E2D8FA24F6B.title: "Crushing Wheels"
	quest.4D980E2D8FA24F6B.quest_subtitle: "Ore doubling"
	quest.4D980E2D8FA24F6B.quest_desc: [
		"Two &6Crushing Wheels&r turning into each other break ore into crushed ore, which"
		"smelts into more than you put in."
		""
		"&7They must turn towards each other, so check the rotation before you power them.&r"
	]
	quest.0AFF29B9B036B17A.title: "Fans"
	quest.0AFF29B9B036B17A.quest_subtitle: "Four processes for one block"
	quest.0AFF29B9B036B17A.quest_desc: [
		"Blow an &6Encased Fan&r through fire and it smelts, through water it washes, through"
		"lava it smokes, and through soul fire it haunts."
		""
		"&7Washing gravel yields flint and iron nuggets; washing soul sand yields quartz and gold.&r"
	]
	quest.7F8EEDF5899104B4.title: "Deployers and Saws"
	quest.7F8EEDF5899104B4.quest_subtitle: "Doing things to a belt"
	quest.7F8EEDF5899104B4.quest_desc: [
		"Whatever passes under a &6Deployer&r gets an item used on it; a &6Mechanical Saw&r cuts"
		"logs and fells trees. A deployer holding a hoe is a farm; holding a sword, it is a mob farm."
	]
	chapter.5867D20584768412.title: "Create"
	chapter.5867D20584768412.chapter_subtitle: ["Cogs, shafts and stress — the mod that makes machines out of moving parts."]
	quest.0AB3E3BC613028C7.title: "Find the Meteorite"
	quest.0AB3E3BC613028C7.quest_subtitle: "Sky stone, and four presses"
	quest.0AB3E3BC613028C7.quest_desc: [
		"AE2 buries &6meteorites&r across the world, each with a chest holding &6Inscriber"
		"Presses&r. Without all four presses the mod stops dead at the inscriber, so keep"
		"looking until you have them."
		""
		"A &6Meteorite Compass&r, charged in a Charger, points at the nearest one."
		""
		"&7The network itself runs along the top of this page and hooks back to the"
		"capstone. Cables and power drop away to the left; autocrafting to the right.&r"
	]
	quest.2A3948347CCC752B.title: "Wireless"
	quest.2A3948347CCC752B.quest_subtitle: "Terminal in your pocket"
	quest.2A3948347CCC752B.quest_desc: [
		"Carry the network in your inventory with a &6Wireless Access Point&r and a &6Wireless"
		"Terminal&r, within range. Range upgrades stack, and Wireless Chargers keep the"
		"terminal topped up."
	]
	quest.052CD5DDC1E1C463.title: "Certus Quartz"
	quest.052CD5DDC1E1C463.quest_subtitle: "The mod's own crystal"
	quest.052CD5DDC1E1C463.quest_desc: [
		"&6Certus Quartz&r generates in the overworld and grows on budding blocks found in"
		"meteorites. A budding block and a powered &6Growth Accelerator&r make the farm."
	]
	quest.682DCD7735B6C0E5.title: "Import and Export"
	quest.682DCD7735B6C0E5.quest_subtitle: "Getting items in and out"
	quest.682DCD7735B6C0E5.quest_desc: [
		"Items come in through an &6Import Bus&r, go out through an &6Export Bus&r, and a"
		"&6Storage Bus&r treats a chest as network storage."
		""
		"&7A Storage Bus on each Warehouse rack puts the colony's stock on your ME terminal.&r"
	]
	quest.4C40B9BEAABE67CA.title: "The Charger"
	quest.4C40B9BEAABE67CA.quest_subtitle: "Charged certus"
	quest.4C40B9BEAABE67CA.quest_desc: [
		"Certus quartz becomes &6Charged Certus Quartz&r in a &6Charger&r, which charges the"
		"meteorite compass while you are there. It needs power; a vibration chamber burning"
		"coal is enough to start."
	]
	quest.46298113943CFD6C.title: "Power It"
	quest.46298113943CFD6C.quest_subtitle: "Energy acceptors and cells"
	quest.46298113943CFD6C.quest_desc: [
		"Power comes in through an &6Energy Acceptor&r from anything and is converted to AE. An"
		"&6Energy Cell&r stores a buffer so the network survives a brownout."
		""
		"&7Create Crafts and Additions is the easiest generator to reach here.&r"
	]
	quest.6010109B26CC22E7.title: "Fluix"
	quest.6010109B26CC22E7.quest_subtitle: "Three things in water"
	quest.6010109B26CC22E7.quest_desc: [
		"Throw &6Charged Certus&r, &6redstone&r and &6nether quartz&r into water and they become"
		"&6Fluix Crystals&r. Every cable and most machines need them."
		""
		"&7It happens in the water, not in a crafting grid.&r"
	]
	quest.4846ABA56376E011.title: "Quartz Glass"
	quest.4846ABA56376E011.quest_subtitle: "And the cables it makes"
	quest.4846ABA56376E011.quest_desc: [
		"&6Quartz Glass&r is glass and certus dust, and &6Fluix Cable&r carries channels between"
		"blocks. Glass cable carries eight channels; dense cable carries thirty-two."
	]
	quest.7D4D66F82F038408.title: "One Wall, Everything In It"
	quest.7D4D66F82F038408.quest_subtitle: "A network that works"
	quest.7D4D66F82F038408.quest_desc: [
		"Controller, drive, cells, terminal and enough power to keep it lit. Every chest in"
		"the base is now one screen."
		""
		"&7A Network Analyser tells you where the channels are going.&r"
	]
	quest.1246B8957DE7B678.title: "The Inscriber"
	quest.1246B8957DE7B678.quest_subtitle: "Where processors are stamped"
	quest.1246B8957DE7B678.quest_desc: [
		"Put a press in each end slot of an &6Inscriber&r and material in the middle and it stamps"
		"out the mod's circuits. Three in a row is the standard setup; one is very slow."
	]
	quest.438CDADFED96DDDD.title: "Drive and Terminal"
	quest.438CDADFED96DDDD.quest_subtitle: "Ten cells, one screen"
	quest.438CDADFED96DDDD.quest_desc: [
		"Ten cells fit in an &6ME Drive&r, and an &6ME Terminal&r is the window you actually use."
		"A Crafting Terminal is the same thing with a crafting grid attached."
	]
	quest.3A0D9A0497DDADD2.title: "Silicon and Processors"
	quest.3A0D9A0497DDADD2.quest_subtitle: "Logic, calculation, engineering"
	quest.3A0D9A0497DDADD2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Silicon&r is smelted from certus dust. Pressed with a circuit and redstone it"
		"becomes a &6Processor&r, in three kinds, all of them needed by the stack, which makes"
		"this the first thing in the mod worth automating."
	]
	quest.6EAED796348C07F6.title: "Spatial Storage"
	quest.6EAED796348C07F6.quest_subtitle: "Move a room"
	quest.6EAED796348C07F6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Spatial Pylons&r around a region and a spatial cell pick the whole thing up and put"
		"it down somewhere else."
		""
		"&7The 2-cube component is banned on this pack for lag. The larger ones are fine.&r"
	]
	quest.082DACCC2712B830.title: "Storage Cells"
	quest.082DACCC2712B830.quest_subtitle: "Housings and components"
	quest.082DACCC2712B830.quest_desc: [
		"Storage cells are a &6Storage Component&r in a &6Cell Housing&r, 1k through 256k, each"
		"holding more of everything but no more kinds."
		""
		"&7Type count matters more than capacity. A 1k cell holds 63 types.&r"
	]
	quest.3962185DE09008E6.title: "The ME Controller"
	quest.3962185DE09008E6.quest_subtitle: "The heart of a network"
	quest.3962185DE09008E6.quest_desc: [
		"An &6ME Controller&r is what makes a network a network. Everything else connects"
		"back to it."
		""
		"&7A controller block may touch neighbours on at most two axes. Build them as a"
		"line or a slab, never a 3D corner.&r"
	]
	quest.464BAD7146F97E65.title: "Formation and Annihilation"
	quest.464BAD7146F97E65.quest_subtitle: "Planes"
	quest.464BAD7146F97E65.quest_desc: [
		"Whatever touches an &6Annihilation Plane&r breaks into the network; a &6Formation Plane&r"
		"places blocks back out. A plane on a quarry face is a very tidy mining setup."
	]
	quest.69E8F96E726734A7.title: "Molecular Assembler"
	quest.69E8F96E726734A7.quest_subtitle: "Crafting, on request"
	quest.69E8F96E726734A7.quest_desc: [
		"One crafting pattern runs in each &6Molecular Assembler&r. Put enough of them beside a"
		"pattern provider and the network builds recipes on demand. Blank patterns are"
		"written at a Pattern Encoding Terminal."
	]
	quest.250BDB9771B0881E.title: "Subnetworks"
	quest.250BDB9771B0881E.quest_subtitle: "When one network is not enough"
	quest.250BDB9771B0881E.quest_desc: [
		"Power passes through a &6Quartz Fiber&r but channels do not, so a small dedicated network"
		"can hang off a big one. Subnets are how large builds stay under their channel budget."
	]
	quest.311FB8CE34942769.title: "Pattern Providers"
	quest.311FB8CE34942769.quest_subtitle: "Where the order goes"
	quest.311FB8CE34942769.quest_desc: [
		"Encoded patterns live in a &6Pattern Provider&r, which hands the ingredients to whatever"
		"is next to it, an assembler or an actual machine."
		""
		"&7Point one at a Create mixer and the network runs Create for you.&r"
	]
	quest.2E16895718A1EE42.title: "Crafting CPU"
	quest.2E16895718A1EE42.quest_subtitle: "The block that plans a craft"
	quest.2E16895718A1EE42.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crafting Units&r with storage and co-processors form a &6Crafting CPU&r, the block"
		"that plans a multi-step craft and runs it. More storage means bigger jobs;"
		"co-processors mean faster ones."
	]
	quest.66FCDB75C52A916C.title: "Ask For a Diamond Pickaxe"
	quest.66FCDB75C52A916C.quest_subtitle: "Autocrafting, working"
	quest.66FCDB75C52A916C.quest_desc: [
		"Type it into the terminal and the network gathers, crafts and delivers. Everything"
		"on this page builds up to this, and a &6Crafting Co-Processing Unit&r is a fair test:"
		"the network has to plan several steps to make one."
		""
		"&7If a craft hangs, look for a missing pattern or a full assembler first.&r"
	]
	chapter.798D35E38124A0F6.title: "Applied Energistics"
	chapter.798D35E38124A0F6.chapter_subtitle: ["A meteorite, four presses, and a warehouse that fits in a wall."]
	quest.5F989F91872F2E86.title: "Materials and You"
	quest.5F989F91872F2E86.quest_subtitle: "The book that comes first"
	quest.5F989F91872F2E86.quest_desc: [
		"&6Materials and You&r is the first of Tinkers' books, and it covers everything up to"
		"your first real tool. You spawn with a copy; a book and a pattern make another."
		""
		"&7The page steps down in three tiers: the workbench along the top, the smeltery"
		"below it, and the foundry and the big tools at the bottom.&r"
	]
	quest.57E4C68E968B4D1A.title: "Patterns"
	quest.57E4C68E968B4D1A.quest_subtitle: "Everything starts here"
	quest.57E4C68E968B4D1A.quest_desc: [
		"Planks and a stick make a &6Pattern&r, and every Tinkers' station block eats one. Make"
		"a handful."
	]
	quest.0920F27AB1313E31.title: "Grout"
	quest.0920F27AB1313E31.quest_subtitle: "Clay, sand and gravel"
	quest.0920F27AB1313E31.quest_desc: [
		"&6Grout&r smelts into &6Seared Bricks&r, and seared brick is what the whole smeltery is"
		"built from. A working smeltery wants hundreds, so make it by the stack."
	]
	quest.4400008707620E93.title: "Seared Bricks"
	quest.4400008707620E93.quest_subtitle: "Smelted grout"
	quest.4400008707620E93.quest_desc: [
		"Grout in a furnace makes &6Seared Brick&r, and four of those make the block. The"
		"smeltery's walls, floor and every fitting are made of it."
		""
		"&7A Seared Melter is the cheap single-block version, and the place to start.&r"
	]
	quest.6263FD3734CB70DC.title: "Melter and Faucet"
	quest.6263FD3734CB70DC.quest_subtitle: "Metal, going somewhere"
	quest.6263FD3734CB70DC.quest_desc: [
		"One thing at a time melts in a &6Seared Melter&r over a heater, and a &6Faucet&r pours it"
		"onto a &6Casting Table&r or into a &6Basin&r. Table for ingots and parts, basin for blocks."
	]
	quest.1D5B43A2E52A4265.title: "The Part Builder"
	quest.1D5B43A2E52A4265.quest_subtitle: "Carving tool parts"
	quest.1D5B43A2E52A4265.quest_desc: [
		"Carve a tool part out of a material at the &6Part Builder&r, using a pattern. Wood and"
		"stone to start, better metals once the smeltery runs, and the book lists every"
		"material's stats."
	]
	quest.7A2B029990C0AD2C.title: "Casts"
	quest.7A2B029990C0AD2C.quest_subtitle: "Gold, spent once"
	quest.7A2B029990C0AD2C.quest_desc: [
		"Pour molten gold over a part on a casting table and it becomes a reusable &6Gold"
		"Cast&r. &6Sand Casts&r are the cheap one-use version."
		""
		"&7Cast the parts you use most: ingot, pickaxe head, handle.&r"
	]
	quest.57E16EF62EC28F5B.title: "The Tinker Station"
	quest.57E16EF62EC28F5B.quest_subtitle: "Assemble a tool"
	quest.57E16EF62EC28F5B.quest_desc: [
		"Parts go together into a tool at the &6Tinker Station&r, and come apart again when you"
		"want to change something. Tools gain levels as you use them, and levels give"
		"modifier slots."
	]
	quest.2A7C961DF065A3C5.title: "The Smeltery"
	quest.2A7C961DF065A3C5.quest_subtitle: "The multiblock proper"
	quest.2A7C961DF065A3C5.quest_desc: [
		"Build a hollow box of seared brick with a &6Smeltery Controller&r in the wall, a drain"
		"and a tank. It melts several things at once and doubles ore."
		""
		"&7Height is capacity, so it is worth building taller than the first job needs.&r"
	]
	quest.7E8E314951DBD592.title: "A Pickaxe You Made"
	quest.7E8E314951DBD592.quest_subtitle: "Head, handle, binding"
	quest.7E8E314951DBD592.quest_desc: [
		"Three parts, three materials, and a tool that is exactly what you chose rather than"
		"what a recipe allowed."
		""
		"&7A broken tool is repaired at the station with its head material, never lost.&r"
	]
	quest.5D137E0DEEF53D42.title: "Alloys"
	quest.5D137E0DEEF53D42.quest_subtitle: "Two metals, one better one"
	quest.5D137E0DEEF53D42.quest_desc: [
		"The smeltery mixes molten metals: copper and amethyst into amethyst bronze, iron and"
		"slime into slimesteel, and so on down the list. Alloying needs both molten at once,"
		"so watch the tank."
	]
	quest.1A26E4A241FE08E2.title: "Modifiers"
	quest.1A26E4A241FE08E2.quest_subtitle: "Where tools get interesting"
	quest.1A26E4A241FE08E2.quest_desc: [
		"Redstone for speed, quartz for damage, lapis for luck, a diamond to raise the"
		"durability ceiling. A &6Tinker's Anvil&r applies the harder ones."
		""
		"&7Modifier slots are finite, so a tool is worth levelling up before they are spent.&r"
	]
	quest.7939761740A73820.title: "Slime and Bone"
	quest.7939761740A73820.quest_subtitle: "Tinkers' own materials"
	quest.7939761740A73820.quest_desc: [
		"&6Necrotic Bone&r for lifesteal, slime for extra durability, and the islands in the"
		"sky where the slime comes from."
		""
		"&7Necrotic bones come off wither skeletons killed with a severing tool.&r"
	]
	quest.519F8B58C997E88A.title: "Scorched Brick"
	quest.519F8B58C997E88A.quest_subtitle: "The Nether smeltery"
	quest.519F8B58C997E88A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Scorched Brick&r builds the &6Foundry&r, the Nether-side version of the smeltery"
		"with better fuel and a different fitting set. It is smelted from Nether Grout: magma,"
		"soul sand and soul soil in place of the clay."
	]
	quest.283250E2824F0905.title: "The Foundry"
	quest.283250E2824F0905.quest_subtitle: "Bigger, and byproducts instead of alloys"
	quest.283250E2824F0905.quest_desc: [
		"The same melting in a scorched box: a &6Foundry Controller&r holds far more metal and"
		"pulls byproducts out of ores. It cannot alloy, so the smeltery stays."
	]
	quest.05965DD04BCDDB1C.title: "A Crafting Station"
	quest.05965DD04BCDDB1C.quest_subtitle: "One workbench for everything"
	quest.05965DD04BCDDB1C.quest_desc: [
		"Place a &6Crafting Station&r against the other Tinkers' blocks and it gives you tabs"
		"across the top, shares their inventories, and remembers the recipe you last used."
	]
	quest.7620649DE1BF4CCD.title: "Tinkers' Integrations"
	quest.7620649DE1BF4CCD.quest_subtitle: "Modded materials, added"
	quest.7620649DE1BF4CCD.quest_desc: [
		"&6TCIntegrations&r adds this pack's other metals to the smeltery: silver, manasteel,"
		"dragonsteel and the rest. A block of Ice and Fire's silver melted"
		"down is the first modded metal most people cast into a tool head."
	]
	quest.3B137E50B0B8B567.title: "A Tool for Everything"
	quest.3B137E50B0B8B567.quest_subtitle: "Broadswords, cleavers, hammers"
	quest.3B137E50B0B8B567.quest_desc: [
		"Past the pickaxe sit the big tools, the &6Cleaver&r, the &6Sledge Hammer&r, the"
		"&6Excavator&r, all assembled the same way from bigger parts."
		""
		"&7A hammer mines three by three and eats durability three times as fast.&r"
	]
	quest.7704AB8F421E2D6C.title: "A Levelled Tool"
	quest.7704AB8F421E2D6C.quest_subtitle: "Modifier slots, all spent"
	quest.7704AB8F421E2D6C.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Sledge Hammer&r built from the best materials the smeltery makes, the largest tool"
		"the mod has, levelled through use and modified at the anvil."
		""
		"&7A Tinkers' tool is rebuilt part by part, so one tool can last the whole pack.&r"
	]
	quest.4CA3972E6990B87B.title: "The Smith's Hall"
	quest.4CA3972E6990B87B.quest_subtitle: "Stations, smeltery and foundry"
	quest.4CA3972E6990B87B.quest_desc: [
		"A crafting station with every Tinkers' block against it, a tall smeltery behind,"
		"and a foundry in the Nether for the rest."
	]
	chapter.59DBA3FC299C11F5.title: "Tinkers' Construct"
	chapter.59DBA3FC299C11F5.chapter_subtitle: ["Grout, seared brick, and a tool you designed rather than crafted."]
	quest.6EB96B048ECBF4A9.title: "Not Just a Chest"
	quest.6EB96B048ECBF4A9.quest_subtitle: "Sophisticated Storage"
	quest.6EB96B048ECBF4A9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sophisticated Storage&r replaces chests and barrels with versions that take"
		"upgrades: sorting, smelting, magnets, filters, pumps."
		""
		"Three panels: the blocks that stay in your base, the backpack that follows you,"
		"and the pipes and odds and ends that move things about. Almost nothing in them"
		"needs anything else first; the first two share an upgrade list."
		""
		"&7The Storage Controller is banned on this pack for lag, so no recipe here uses it.&r"
	]
	quest.5918E4D9A99F9F04.title: "Pipez"
	quest.5918E4D9A99F9F04.quest_subtitle: "One pipe, four contents"
	quest.5918E4D9A99F9F04.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pipez&r moves items, fluids, energy and gas, with a wrench to configure each face"
		"and upgrades to make it faster. A Universal Pipe carries all four at once."
	]
	quest.08DBDBCA063937E2.title: "A Better Barrel"
	quest.08DBDBCA063937E2.quest_subtitle: "Wood, then metal"
	quest.08DBDBCA063937E2.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Storage Chest&r or &6Barrel&r starts at twenty-seven slots and one upgrade slot"
		"and climbs from there. A Limited Barrel holds fewer types but many more of each."
	]
	quest.258D3F65E54D7321.title: "Everything Where It Should Be"
	quest.258D3F65E54D7321.quest_subtitle: "A base that files itself"
	quest.258D3F65E54D7321.quest_desc: [
		"Filtered barrels along a wall and a backpack that keeps itself stocked."
		""
		"Applied Energistics does the same job a different way. Both are correct."
	]
	quest.02482ADCEC71E11D.title: "Pipe Upgrades"
	quest.02482ADCEC71E11D.quest_subtitle: "Basic to ultimate"
	quest.02482ADCEC71E11D.quest_desc: [
		"Each upgrade tier raises how much a pipe moves per operation and how many filter"
		"slots the face has."
		""
		"&7Filter at the destination rather than the source. It is easier to reason about.&r"
	]
	quest.4AE8D53C4333C1E1.title: "Tier Upgrades"
	quest.4AE8D53C4333C1E1.quest_subtitle: "Copper, iron, gold, diamond, netherite"
	quest.4AE8D53C4333C1E1.quest_desc: [
		"Apply a &6Tier Upgrade&r to a storage block and it gains slots and upgrade slots without"
		"being unloaded first. Upgrades skip tiers, so a basic-to-diamond exists and saves materials."
	]
	quest.163725A0293DB910.title: "Smelt In Place"
	quest.163725A0293DB910.quest_subtitle: "Furnace upgrades"
	quest.163725A0293DB910.quest_desc: [
		"&6Auto Smelting&r, &6Smoking&r and &6Blasting&r upgrades turn a barrel into a furnace"
		"that keeps its own output. Fuel goes in the same block."
	]
	quest.3FB2EDE14F6BC8D1.title: "Wireless Chargers"
	quest.3FB2EDE14F6BC8D1.quest_subtitle: "No cable to the terminal"
	quest.3FB2EDE14F6BC8D1.quest_desc: [
		"Powered items stay topped up near a &6Wireless Charger&r: a block one for machines, a"
		"player one for whatever you carry. It pairs with the AE2 wireless terminal, which"
		"otherwise runs flat."
	]
	quest.0510940BEAB6FE2A.title: "Stacks of Stacks"
	quest.0510940BEAB6FE2A.quest_subtitle: "Stack upgrades"
	quest.0510940BEAB6FE2A.quest_desc: [
		"Each slot holds more with a &6Stack Upgrade&r fitted: five tiers and an omega tier past"
		"those. With one fitted, a single barrel holds an entire mining trip of cobblestone."
	]
	quest.597D3290E9060161.title: "Compact and Void"
	quest.597D3290E9060161.quest_subtitle: "The two housekeeping upgrades"
	quest.597D3290E9060161.quest_desc: [
		"&6Compacting&r turns nine of a thing into its block automatically. &6Void&r throws away"
		"anything over a threshold you set, so the cobblestone barrel never overflows."
	]
	quest.54676119260DC1BA.title: "Dark Utilities"
	quest.54676119260DC1BA.quest_subtitle: "Plates, charms and filters"
	quest.54676119260DC1BA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Dark Utilities&r is a box of small tricks: pressure plates that damage or slow,"
		"charms that ward off insomnia and bad effects, and mob filters for farms."
		""
		"&7Its filters are how a mob farm kills one kind of thing and not the rest.&r"
	]
	quest.189190B4302E3EA3.title: "Sort It Yourself"
	quest.189190B4302E3EA3.quest_subtitle: "Filter and hopper upgrades"
	quest.189190B4302E3EA3.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Hopper Upgrade&r pulls from the block on one side and pushes into the block on the"
		"other, and a &6Filter Upgrade&r decides what it accepts. A row of filtered barrels is"
		"a sorting system with no redstone in it."
	]
	quest.0953065E0C7BB1F3.title: "Sharestones"
	quest.0953065E0C7BB1F3.quest_subtitle: "Waystones, shared"
	quest.0953065E0C7BB1F3.quest_desc: [
		"Anyone can use a &6Sharestone&r, colour-coded so a server's network stays readable."
		"Bound Scrolls jump to one fixed stone; Warp Scrolls jump to any of them."
	]
	quest.612E3FBC0C6B2C18.title: "Upgrading the Backpack"
	quest.612E3FBC0C6B2C18.quest_subtitle: "Same upgrades, on your back"
	quest.612E3FBC0C6B2C18.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Backpack&r takes the same family of upgrades and travels with you."
		""
		"&7The Pickup Upgrade is the first slot most people fill: drops go straight into the pack.&r"
	]
	quest.5B20AB197FB097C4.title: "Feed and Refill"
	quest.5B20AB197FB097C4.quest_subtitle: "Two upgrades worth the slot"
	quest.5B20AB197FB097C4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Feeding&r eats for you when hunger drops; &6Refill&r keeps your hotbar topped up from"
		"the backpack. Feeding plus a stack of cooked food ends food management entirely."
	]
	quest.5590C330EBD31241.title: "Restock and Deposit"
	quest.5590C330EBD31241.quest_subtitle: "Building and unloading"
	quest.5590C330EBD31241.quest_desc: [
		"&6Restock&r refills the stack in your hand from the backpack as you place, so a long"
		"wall never needs a hotbar reload. &6Deposit&r empties the pack into whatever you"
		"are standing at."
	]
	quest.45246BBB9A4CDBDB.title: "Magnets"
	quest.45246BBB9A4CDBDB.quest_subtitle: "Pull drops to you"
	quest.45246BBB9A4CDBDB.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Magnet Upgrade&r pulls drops to you from several blocks away, and with the pickup"
		"upgrade already fitted they go straight into the pack."
		""
		"&7Filter the pickup, or the backpack fills with cobblestone.&r"
	]
	quest.26F42366AD10352B.title: "Tools and Anvils"
	quest.26F42366AD10352B.quest_subtitle: "The odd ones"
	quest.26F42366AD10352B.quest_desc: [
		"Repairs happen from inside the backpack with an &6Anvil Upgrade&r, and a &6Tool Swapper&r"
		"picks the right tool for the block you are hitting. Both remove an errand you had stopped noticing."
	]
	quest.7A159EFFDB01B138.title: "Filters, Properly"
	quest.7A159EFFDB01B138.quest_subtitle: "Item Filters"
	quest.7A159EFFDB01B138.quest_desc: [
		"&6Item Filters&r adds filter items that match by tag, by mod, by damage or by a"
		"regular expression, and they slot into every filter upgrade on this page."
		""
		"&7A #forge:ores filter in one barrel replaces twenty individual entries.&r"
	]
	chapter.0A8A9C4CBCD305E8.title: "Storage and Logistics"
	chapter.0A8A9C4CBCD305E8.chapter_subtitle: ["Barrels that upgrade, backpacks that sort themselves, and pipes between them."]
